    "synthesis": "# Corpus Index — 9-Agent Adversarial Audit Synthesis\n\n**Scope:** every code path that produces, reads, or transports `corpus/index/compiled-index.json`.\n**Baseline:** working tree, branch `feat/wraith-retrieval`. All line numbers resolve against the **dirty working tree** (`scripts/compile-corpus-index.py` = 1,412 lines; `compiled-index.json` = 701 nodes / 72 hooks / 64 tensions / 1,722 terms / 664,494 bytes). Spot-verified during synthesis.\n**Findings:** 353 raw → 56 CONFIRMED after adversarial verification, 7 REFUTED, deduplicated below to **48 distinct defects**.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The defect register\n\n### 1a. CONFIRMED — CRITICAL\n\n| Sev | Category | path:line | Defect | Failure scenario | Consequence | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CRIT | error-swallowing | `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:14-15`, `:153-154` | Docstring promises \"Malformed rows/entries are skipped with warnings to stderr.\" `warn()` is the only stderr writer in 1,412 lines and emits **0 bytes** on the live corpus. All 12 `warn()` sites sit inside `except Exception` handlers or missing-file guards; the 23 real discard sites are bare `continue`/`return None`, which raise nothing and open nothing, so no handler can ever fire. | Full read-only run of `collect_ontology_nodes` + `collect_cross_pipeline_hooks` + `collect_tension_edges` + `deduplicate_ontology_nodes` + `build_canonical_terms` with stderr captured → `''`. Meanwhile 70 nodes absorbed, 55 tension records dropped, 23,843 chars truncated, 18 de-anima claim rows discarded. | The only mechanism the author has for noticing the index is eating their work is disabled by construction. Every other finding in this report is invisible to the operator, indefinitely. | ~60 lines: module `ERRORS` counter in `warn()`, call at every discard site with path+line, print in summary, `--strict` → `sys.exit(1)` |\n| CRIT | silent-data-loss | `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:260-261` | `if len(cells) < 5: continue` drops every markdown table row with <5 pipe-cells. No warn, no counter, no trace. Note `:270` already lists `\"targeted concept\"` as a recognized header — a later guard silently vetoed an earlier feature. | `corpus/index/Aristotle - Complete Works/de-anima-ontology.md:57` opens a 4-column table **inside** the 3A slice. 18 rows dropped vs 28 kept, including the KP1–KP10 \"Key Positions\" table carrying Bekker loci. Relaxing only the threshold to `<4` recovers all rows (25→31 nodes), proving `:260` is the sole gate. | Claim-level records with citation loci vanish. Verified: `\"431a17\"`, `\"429a27\"`, `\"Place of forms\"`, `\"topos eidōn\"` all return **0 hits** in the shipped artifact. Under the standing *gross advisor-rigor for citations* rule this is citation-fatal. | ~10 lines warn; ~40 for width-aware dispatch |\n| CRIT | wrong-output | `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:718-721` | `elif current_key and stripped:` (absorb) precedes `elif stripped.startswith(\"###\") or ...: break` (terminate). Once any field is open, `current_key` is never reset, so the terminator is dead. Blank lines don't help — all four arms are false for `\"\"`. | Instrumented over all 17 header files: **absorb-arm 108 hits / 21,879 chars; break-arm 0 hits.** The last `**N.` section of any header-format file runs to EOF. Absorbed `- **X**:` lines *re-open* field keys, so pollution lands in whichever field is open last. | Two shipped nodes corrupt. `Preparatory Rhetoric` (Rickert): `centralityTier` = **10,009 chars** of the Section 3B global edge list, `units` = **973 tokens**, node = 20,377 bytes = 3.07% of the whole artifact. `Temporalität` (BT): 247 chars / 586 units, and its units are wrongly inherited from tension T8 — the prompt emits `[D1-U1, D1-U5, D1-U8, D2-U2, D2-U3]` where the source says `Intro-U2, D2-U6`. That is a **plausible-looking, 100%-wrong provenance assertion** with no garbage token to tip anyone off. | 5 lines to reorder; correct fix is byte-bounded sections |\n| CRIT | wrong-output | `src/god-agent/shared/cross-author-utils.ts:473-474` | `normalizedTopics.some(t => targetLower.includes(t) \\|\\| t.includes(targetLower))` — with `targetConcept === ''`, `t.includes('')` is **always true** in JS. 31 of 72 hooks have an empty `targetConcept` (verified). | Facet topic words `['zzzzz','qqqqqq']` push **31 of 72 hooks** into `activeBridges`, all matched solely via `t.includes('')`. Same 31 for `['boredom','attunement','pedagogy']`. | `getActiveBridges` is not a matcher; it is a near-constant function. Cross-author bridging as a feature does not exist — it is noise injection, and has never worked on this corpus. | ~4 lines guard; correct fix is schema rejection at load |\n| CRIT | wrong-output | `cross-author-utils.ts:498` → `src/god-agent/universal/gold-standard-prompt-builder.ts:712-716` | `activeBridges.slice(0, 1)` after the always-match above selects, for most topics, `hook-de-anima-07` — whose `targetText`, `targetConcept`, `bridge` and `relevance` are **all empty strings**. | Three unrelated topic sets all return `hook-de-anima-07`. The rendered prompt reads: `**Bridge [hook-de-anima-07]:** Summary Matrix (Aristotle) ↔ ? (Unknown)` followed by `Both authors (Aristotle and Unknown) MUST be cited with direct textual evidence`. | A **mandatory, high-confidence-framed instruction to fabricate a cross-author synthesis with a non-existent author**, injected into the drafting prompt for a doctoral dissertation. \"Summary Matrix\" is a markdown heading the compiler mistook for a concept. Single most fabrication-inducing line in the read path. | ~15 lines across 2 files + upstream hook repair |\n| CRIT | uninvalidated-cache | `cross-author-utils.ts:56`, `:342`, `:351` | `let _hooksDerivationDone = false;` — one-shot module global. `grep -rn` over `src/`, `tests/`, `scripts/` returns **exactly those 3 lines**; no reset exists anywhere. Meanwhile `jsonl-loaders.ts:205-213` invalidates on mtime and returns a **freshly parsed** object. 0 of 72 hooks carry `sourceAuthor` on disk, so derivation at `:344-349` is the only source. | Daemon calls `getActiveBridges` once. Someone recompiles. mtime changes. Fresh parse, flag still true, derivation skipped forever. | Two silent failures: (a) `icp-orchestrator.ts:368` `if (requiredAuthors.size < 2) continue;` fires — cross-author retrieval backfill dies, and `:364` has *already logged* \"Bridge activated\", so the trace reads as success; (b) `gold-standard-prompt-builder.ts:712-715` interpolates `undefined`, so the prompt literally reads `Summary Matrix (undefined) ↔ ? (undefined)`. | ~6 lines: delete the flag, derive lazily per hook |\n| CRIT | error-swallowing | `src/god-agent/shared/jsonl-loaders.ts:202`, `:215-217` | The only sanctioned reader of `compiled-index.json` wraps `statSync`+`readFileSync`+`JSON.parse` in `} catch { return null; }` — no log, no counter, no distinction between absent / permission-denied / corrupt. | Compiler mid-write; `JSON.parse` throws → `null` → `cross-author-utils.ts:339` returns null → `getActiveBridges` `[]` → `corpus-index-provider.ts:106` returns three empty arrays → `retrieval-stage.ts:477` logs **only when arrays are non-empty**. | Total ontology/hook/tension blackout for an entire session, **zero log lines**, normal-looking draft. Widest blast radius and least observability in the whole read path. | ~8 lines |\n| CRIT | wrong-output | `cross-author-utils.ts:317` | `buildCorpusCatalog` defaults every title with a missing `authority_tier` to `'secondary'`. | 71 of 117 catalog titles mislabelled — including Heidegger's *Fundamental Concepts of Metaphysics* (source text of the entire boredom analysis) and the Greek critical editions of *De Anima*, *Physica*, *Ars Rhetorica*. Injected via `llm-decomposition-provider.ts:102-103`. | The model is told the dissertation's primary texts are secondary scholarship. Directly attacks the primary/secondary distinction the citation rigor depends on. 61% of the catalog is wrong. | ~6 lines (emit `UNCLASSIF