üll format writes the same value into `dependencyRelation` **and** `conflictRelation` and drops the label. All 10 Uexküll edges assert a fabricated symmetry. |\n| MED | `compile-corpus-index.py:1299-1301` | Tests length of the **raw** translation, adds the **stripped** value → can emit a 1-char and even an **empty-string** canonical term (proven). `includes('')` is universally true downstream. |\n| MED | `compile-corpus-index.py:1276-1304` | 165 terms ≥40 chars (max 118: `'Debate axis 9: … ↔ effects inconsistent/assumed-not-demonstrated'`); 20 contain `:` or `↔`. Meanwhile **13 terms <4 chars are unreachable** by the only consumer's `t.length >= 4` filter — including `ὕλη`, `ἁφή`, `φῶς`. Bloated with strings no query contains; missing the Greek lemmas the dissertation is about. |\n| MED | `compile-corpus-index.py:166-168` | `strip_bold` removes only `**`. **35 nodes ship with literal asterisks** (`'*Umwelt*'` as a canonical term that can never match `Umwelt`). |\n| MED | `compile-corpus-index.py:1352-1356` | Docstring promises M-05 filtering of definition-less nodes; code only `print()`s a count — **to stdout**, not via `warn()`. `2>/dev/null` still shows it; `1>/dev/null` hides it. The one diagnostic that fires is on the wrong stream. |\n| MED | `compile-corpus-index.py:282-287`, `:314-319` | Both warn-bearing `try/except` blocks are **dead** — neither `_parse_table_row` nor `_parse_field_value_section` can raise on any input (all indices width-guarded). The sites the docstring describes are structurally incapable of executing. |\n| MED | `jsonl-loaders.ts:224` | `_authorKUIndexCache` stores `mtimeMs` but omits the `path` field every neighbouring cache carries → two project roots sharing an mtime return each other's index. |\n| MED | `jsonl-loaders.ts:49`, `:207`, `:258`, `:281` | Every cache hands out the **live object by reference**, unfrozen. One consumer (`cross-author-utils.ts:345`) already mutates it — and that mutation is load-bearing, so the two decisions are entangled. |\n| MED | `corpus-index-provider.ts:73-77`, `:200-202` | `loadCompiledIndex(indexPath)` and `getCompiledIndex(indexPath)` **accept an index path and silently ignore it**. Blocks the obvious route to reproducible drafting (pin a snapshot) and would produce confidently wrong provenance if anyone tried. |\n| MED | `cross-author-utils.ts:382` vs `:338`; `corpus-index-provider.ts:76` | `projectRoot` honoured inconsistently → mixed-root view, single-slot cache thrashing, and **the undefined-author bug fires on the second call** rather than after a recompile. |\n| MED | `cross-author-utils.ts:395-403` | `deriveAuthor`'s dash branch returns a raw slice **without** manifest resolution, contradicting its own docstring; the final fallback returns the first manifest author whose ≥5-char key appears as a substring, **in Map insertion order**. Works today only because every hook is Aristotle. `'Heidegger'` ≠ manifest `'Heidegger, Martin'` → `whereFilter: {author_raw: {$eq:'Heidegger'}}` returns zero rows. |\n| MED | `cross-author-utils.ts:613` vs `:461`, `:517` | Producer keeps words ≥4; both consumers discard <5. `'soul'`, `'body'`, `'mind'`, `'nous'`, `'doxa'`, `'time'`, `'form'` — the load-bearing four-letter vocabulary of this dissertation — structurally excluded, and the exclusion looks identical to \"no bridge is relevant.\" |\n| MED | `cross-author-utils.ts:489` | Tag-confidence tie-break tests for `'medium'`, but every medium hook is tagged `'INTERP-med'` → scores 0, same as low. Ties fall to `localeCompare(id)` — **alphabetical ID order outranks confidence**. |\n| MED | `corpus-index-provider.ts:81-91`, `:118` | `scoreCandidate` counts raw substring occurrences, global regex, no boundary, no length normalization → **ranking dominated by definition length**. 37 candidates tie at the cutoff with no secondary key, so which 12 of 44 reach the prompt is fixed by array order in the JSON — which the compiler reshuffles between builds. |\n| MED | `god_learn.py:389-408`, `:368-377`, `:87-109` | `normalize_knowledge_store` swallows decode errors while rebuilding `index.json` offsets and reports `N` KUs / `M` offsets with `N != M` unflagged — invoked as an *autofix*. `row_id` falls back to `json.dumps(sort_keys=True)`, so an id-less KU is ordered by content and any edit shifts every subsequent byte offset. Contradictions grouped by an **unordered frozenset**, so `A supports B` + `B contrasts_with A` is a false hard contradiction that would `SystemExit(1)` — and the message names the pair alphabetically, omitting the directions needed to adjudicate. |\n| MED | `god_learn.py:680-708`, `:751-808` | `deduplicate_manifest` reads the whole 1.08 MB manifest into memory and rewrites it **non-atomically** with `write_text`, no backup, silently dropping malformed lines. `main()` always returns 0 — `cmd_status` and `cmd_compile` have no failure path at all. |\n| MED | `reason_over_knowledge.py:46-51` vs `:121-156` | **8 of 15 `CANONICAL_RELATIONS` can never be emitted** (`depends_on`, `operationalizes`, `completes`, `defined_by`, `instantiates`, `is_meaning_of`, `is_species_of`, `is_principle_of`), so the filter at `:309-310` is a no-op. Meanwhile the CSVs use `depends_on` 382× and `is_meaning_of` 62×. Relation labels are decided by the order of five `if`s; `DEFINITION_MARKERS` contains bare `'means'`, so **\"by means of\" produces `defined_as` edges**. |\n| MED | `reason_over_knowledge.py:420-441` | `prune_top_k_per_unit` unions per-unit top-k keep-sets, so it does **not** cap degree at k, contradicting `:278` and the CLI help at `:486`. |\n| MED | `scripts/normalize-edges.py:78-96`, `:266-275`, `:127-129` | 8 distinct Aristotle weights (0.60…1.0) collapse to 2 buckets; `'medium'` conflates real 0.5-0.79 with *absent*. Dedup drops the losing row entirely, and is only reported under `--stats`/`--all`. `row.get(k,\"\").strip()` raises `AttributeError` (no filename, no line) on any short row — the other four resolvers are None-safe. |\n| MED | `scripts/verify-hardening.ts:118-125` | The **only** executable check over the read path is in neither CI nor `package.json`, and its bridge assertion passes **by luck** — it uses the one query in the corpus containing a literal German word sitting in a `targetConcept`. Change the query and it would surface the `Unknown`-author bug. False assurance on the most broken behaviour. |\n| MED | `tests/data-integrity/test_reasoning_edges.py:73-78` | The only automated check on the artifact is **tautological** — it asserts the postcondition of the dict used to build the array. The 70 absorbed nodes, 14,066 discarded chars, 34 flipped tiers and 55 dropped tensions all leave it green. So would an artifact with one node. |\n| LOW | `compile-corpus-index.py:157-163` | latin-1 fallback **cannot fail** — mojibake Greek would flow into names and canonicalTerms as terms matching nothing, with one warn per file, not per poisoned term. |\n| LOW | `compile-corpus-index.py:32` | Output written **inside** the scanned tree, and `SKIP_DIRS` doesn't exclude `corpus/index` → the 664 KB derived artifact can be ingested as a source document. |\n| LOW | `compile-corpus-index.py:1397-1404` | The only per-text accounting mixes 30 merged composite labels into the counts. *Aristotle – De Anima* shows 11 nodes; it contributed 20. Unparseable and wrong for exactly the shared concepts that matter most. |\n| LOW | `compile-corpus-index.py:1384-1387` | Single monolithic pretty-printed JSON; `indent=2` alone costs **137,323 bytes (20.7%)**; Node parses it in 3.8 ms for **5.7 MB heap — 8.6× expansion** — and does so twice. |\n| LOW | `merge-reasoning-edges.py:17-23`, `:92-93` | Every path is a module constant; no argparse, no `--dry-run`, always destructive. `BACKUP_EDGES` is the **only** input with no `exists()` guard and points at `tmp/backup-pre-ku-plan-2026-03-18/` — a scratch directory holding the human-curated ground truth. |\n| LOW | `normalize-edges.py:71-75`, `:174-189` | 48-bit truncated edge ids (~0.7% birthday collision at 2M edges) excluding `note`/`units`; `write_jsonl` omits `note` when empty → 8-key and 9-key records in one file. |\n| LOW | `cross-author-utils.ts:307-331` | `buildCorpusCatalog` is the **one** component that scales linearly with the corpus — 8,439 chars today, ~844 KB / ~211,000 tokens at 100x, injected uncapped into every decomposition prompt. Hard wall at ~90x. |\n| LOW | `corpus-index-provider.ts:10-11`, `:86` vs `:162-164`, `:29-50` vs `cross-author-utils.ts:20-45` | Two unused fs imports; regex escaping implemented twice with divergent semantics (`gi` no-boundary vs `i` boundary); `CrossPipelineHook`, `TensionEdge` and `CompiledIndex` each declared twice with different shapes. **There is no single authoritative type for the index** — the structural precondition for the `sourceAuthor: string` unsoundness. |\n\n### 1d. REFUTED — the honest record\n\n| Original claim | path:line | Why refuted | Residual |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `_parse_header_tables` 3A-only window loses 153 rows — HIGH silent-data-loss | `compile-corpus-index.py:554-560` | The window is **deliberate and protective**. 91 of the 153 rows are edge/tension/summary tables that must never become nodes; simulating the \"fix\" fabricates **62 nodes named `depends_on`, `presupposes`, `contrasts_with`**. The headline scenario is false: HR's 33-row canonical table is *not* lost — `parse_header_ontology`'s independent path at `:533-536` harvests it and all 36 rows resolve in the artifact (HR ships 30 nodes). Both consequences misattributed: `Contributors` is absent because `_parse_uexkull_table_row:627-674` has no such field, not because of the window; the missing hooks are caused solely by `:1239`. Precision error: the regex **does** match for all four files; the empty return comes from `:569-570`. | LOW — unlogged empty return; ~19 rows genuinely never ingested; 1 concept name (`Attunement`) missing |\n| `normalize_row` fabricates 8,889 blank triples (43.1%) — CRITICAL | `normalize-edges.py:125-144` | Wrong metric: 8,889 is \"any one field empty\"; **actual blank triples = 895 (4.3%)**. Neither figure is reachable — `--all` touches 6 files / 793 rows, all with full triples, `blank_triples = 0`. The reporter bypassed the CLI; through the real entry point `detect_pipeline` returns None and `parser.error` **exits 2** on exactly that input. Dedup collapses 45 identical blanks to 1. And there is no downstream: **zero callers repo-wide, and `git ls-files` shows the file is UNTRACKED.** | The real problem is the inverse — a dead stub reaching 3.8% of rows (already logged as CRITICAL coverage) |\n| Merge is non-idempotent, destroying manual-edge provenance — CRITICAL | `merge-reasoning-edges.py:123-125` | Mechanism real, harm false. `:174` places manual edges **first** and `:195` uses a strict `>`, so ties keep the first index — the re-tagged copy is discarded at `:200`. Three-run simulation: 788 `manual` + 33 `bridge` survive with `generation_epoch=0`; **exactly 2 edges change derivation, ZERO change epoch**; run 3 == run 2 (fixpoint). The hand-curated/machine boundary is precisely what *is* preserved. | MEDIUM. **But the reporter aimed at the wrong file:** run 2 truncates `unanchored-edges.jsonl` from **1,141 records to 0** via the unconditional `\"w\"` at `:211-213`. Unrecoverable. Independently HIGH. |\n| `cmd_verify` destroys 248 failed index rows — CRITICAL | `god_learn.py:711-718` | Numbers reproduce exactly; the defect does not. **All 248 removed failed rows have a strictly later `ok` row for the identical `path_abs`** (248/248); rows whose failure is the *current* state and would be destroyed: **zero**. Two `status='failed'` rows **survive** — falsifying \"a manifest that says everything is ok\". Not silent: `:702-706` prints and logs `\"manifest dedup: 1182 -> 696 (486 duplicates removed)\"`. Not the only record: the file is git-tracked; 300 of 486 removed lines recoverable from HEAD. | LOW — a command named `verify` mutating its input is a hygiene smell; `:701` non-atomic write is a separate real issue |\n| `clearJSONLCaches()` is a loaded gun with a live caller path — CRITICAL | `jsonl-loaders.ts:305-310` | The project is **ESM** (`\"type\":\"module\"`, `module: NodeNext`, static imports at `quality-integration.ts:32-53`). `require` is not a binding: calling `clearEdgeCache()` throws `ReferenceError: require is not defined` before reaching `clearJSONLCaches`. The claim's own scenario concedes zero callers; `clearEdgeCache` doesn't exist in `dist/` at all. And a plain recompile reaches the identical corrupt state *without* any cache-clear — so fixing this as written would not fix the reachable bug. | LOW. **Bonus real finding:** the identical broken `require` at `quality-integration.ts:749` sits in a `try{…}catch{/* non-fatal */}` closing at `:764`, so it throws on **every** call, is swallowed, and `detectUnanchoredEdges` runs with `ontologyExpansion` permanently empty — no Greek/transliteration/alias expansion, ever, zero log output. Always-on silent degradation. |\n| `run_ingest.py` skip predicate traps 531 phase-less records forever | `run_ingest.py:167-171` | Phase 1 **has no vectors to give** (`:13`, `:352`) — the skip is orthogonal to the no-vector state. Not stuck: replaying the real `should_skip_phase2` over the real manifest gives **0 skipped, 531 processed**. Phase 2 does its own `rglob` (`:982`) and consults the manifest only per-file (`:1141`); a Phase-1 `continue` cannot dequeue anything. `--force` (`:842`) exists. The proposed fix is **actively harmful** — it would re-append all 531 records on every run, unbounded. | LOW/cosmetic — a `status:\"ok\"` phase-less row reads as \"fully ingested\" to a reader not also checking `phase` |\n| `corpus/index` absent from immutability protection — HIGH | `immutability_checker.py:111-122` | Load-bearing arithmetic wrong: the checker never hashes the directory; `:296-297` skips anything not in the 24-entry baseline → **15 files / 43.5 MB hashed, not 1.5 GB** (98.7% of the \"over-protected\" directory is itself unprotected). Not \"zero protection\": the artifact is git-tracked (335 files under `corpus/index`) and the reporter's own proof is `git status` detecting it. The remedy is **harmful** — `:1375` stamps a fresh `builtAt` every run, so a SHA baseline would be red 100% of the time. The scenario (\"400 nodes instead of 701\") demands a *regression* detector; a hash baseline is a binary equality test that cannot express magnitude. And `god-learn-qa.yml:5-21` doesn't list `corpus/**`, so it never fires anyway. | LOW, and **relocated**: there is no count/schema/magnitude gate on the artifact anywhere in CI, and the one test that touches it is unwired. That belongs against CI wiring, not this file. |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Prior-claim reconciliation\n\n| # | Prior claim | Verdict | Correction |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 17 in-branch discard sites (22 with structural), at `:260 :346 :430 :546 :559 :596 :650 :690 :727 :827 :837 :1110 :1120 :1128 :1267 :1290 :1300`; earlier audit said 7 | **PARTIAL — undercount** | All 17 verified verbatim. But **lines 1-520 alone contain ≥20**, and 500-1000 contains **9 more** not listed (`:539-540`, `:569-570`, `:588-592`, `:606`, `:611-614`, `:661`, `:666/:667/:672`, `:714-717`, `:756-767`). True total is well above 22. The **largest single loss is not on the list**: `:308`'s unbounded split (9,867 chars). |\n| 2 | Zero `warn()` calls while discarding 55 tension records; docstring `:14-15` promises warnings | **CONFIRMED** | Stronger than stated. Root cause named for the first time: all 12 `warn()` sites are in `except`/missing-file guards; the 23 discard sites are bare `continue`/`return None` and can never reach a handler. The `:1356` \"WARNING\" is a bare `print()` to **stdout**. |\n| 3 | No `sys.exit`, no counter, no `--strict`, no argparse; `main()` at `:1361` always returns 0 | **CONFIRMED** | `grep -cE \"argparse\\|sys\\.exit\\|assert \\|--strict\"` = **0**. `main() -> None` at `:1361`; `:1411-1412` is bare `main()`, not `sys.exit(main())`. No `assert` anywhere. |\n| 4 | `:1375` stamps `builtAt` unconditionally → byte-identical runs impossible | **CONFIRMED** | Understated. Even removing `builtAt` would not give byte-identical runs — term **order** also varies per process (see #5). Additional: `builtAt` is declared at `corpus-index-provider.ts:53` and **read by nothing**, so it guarantees non-reproducible builds while providing zero provenance. |\n| 5 | `canonicalTerms` sorts on `(-len, lower())`; 101 case-duplicate pairs tie and flip per run | **CONFIRMED** | Exactly 101 tie groups / 202 terms. Five processes → five digests. A fresh compile differs from the shipped file in **106 of 1,722 positions**. Additional: the sort's stated purpose (greedy matching) **has no consumer** — `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:268-270` uses an order- and case-insensitive `includes` filter. The sort is pure diff-churn. |\n| 6 | `deduplicate_ontology_nodes:1319-1321` keys on `name.lower()`; `:1331-1332` concatenates provenance; 771→701, 70 absorbed, no per-merge log | **CONFIRMED** | Understated. **All 51 collisions are cross-text, zero within a text.** 45 groups had conflicting tier/type; **14,066 chars of definition discarded**; in **32 of 51** the surviving definition and surviving greek/type/tier come from different books. `type`/`centralityTier` are never merged at all, so the **first book in `TEXT_DIRS` order dictates both — and Part III secondary clusters are listed first**, systematically demoting primary sources (`das Man`, `Pathos`, `Kairos`, `Enthymeme` all lose to Boredom Secondary). |\n| 7 | Unreachable break at `:718-721`; the last field of the last node in **ANY** header section absorbs the rest of the file; one `centralityTier` = 10,009 chars / 973 units | **PARTIAL** | Mechanism exact; three corrections. (a) The break **is** live in one window — before the first field — where it drops the whole node via `:727-728`. (b) Unit of absorption is the **split section**, not the file, so only the file's last section reaches EOF: **2 of 17 files affected**, not \"ANY\". (c) Absorbed text does **not** stay in one field — `- **X**:` lines re-open keys. **Undercount:** a *second* polluted node exists (`Temporalität`, 247 chars / 586 units), and the cited \"next largest node: 1,300 bytes\" is wrong — it is 7,024 bytes and is the same bug. |\n| 8 | The string `\"ontology.json\"` appears nowhere in 1,412 lines | **CONFIRMED** | `grep -c` = 0. **Sharpened, and this is decisive for §7:** **12 `*-ontology.json` files exist under `corpus/index`.** *Heidegger and Rhetoric*'s is **56,912 bytes** with structured `canonical_nodes` (incl. `contributors` and `cross_pipeline_links`), `contested_concepts` with per-contributor readings, and `tension_summary` — none recoverable from the markdown scrape. **The compiler regex-scrapes prose while the structured twin sits in the same directory.** |\n| 9 | `parse_ontology_md` does not exist; real entries are `parse_table_ontology:195`, `parse_header_ontology:513`, `_parse_field_value_ontology:292` | **CONFIRMED** | Exact. Dispatch at `:1196`/`:1217`, with `:216-217` rerouting table→field/value. **The handoff document names a function that has never existed.** |\n| 10 | `:1239` hardcodes `aristotle_dir`; `:1239-1244` globs hooks under it only → all 72 hooks Aristotle | **CONFIRMED** | 9 hook files exist, all in that directory. Additional: those 72 hooks are largely **hollow** — 66 empty `relevance`, 31 empty `targetConcept`, 15 empty `targetText`, 0 with `sourceAuthor`. |\n| 11 | `_normalize_tension_edge` guard `:1128-1129`; 4 of 11 tension files yield zero | **CONFIRMED** | Exact: Burke GM 16, Calleja 12, Gross 15, Wendt 12 = 55 lost of 119. All four unwrap fine at `:1098-1101`, so not even the `:1104` warning fires. **Additional:** 8 further registered entries have **no tension file at all** and `:1268 if tension_file.is_file():` has no `else` — unlike the ontology loop at `:1228`. All 7 Part III clusters contribute zero tensions, silently. |\n| 12 | `_hooksDerivationDone` one-shot, no reset; recompile empties `requiredAuthors`; `icp-orchestrator.ts:368` continues; backfill dies **with no log line** | **PARTIAL** | Line numbers exact; `grep` returns exactly 3 lines. **Two corrections, both worse.** (a) \"No log line\" is wrong and the truth is worse: `:364` **logs \"Bridge activated\"** immediately before the `continue`, so the trace reads as success. (b) Recompile is not the only trigger — `clearJSONLCaches()` and any non-cwd `projectRoot` (which thrashes the single-slot cache) fire it on the **second call**. Also the downstream effect isn't only the ICP continue: `gold-standard-prompt-builder.ts:712-715` renders literal `undefined`. |\n| 13 | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:794` is a second uninvalidated cache; `:798` re-reads and re-parses the index | **PARTIAL — off by one** | `:794` is the signature; the uninvalidated guard is **`:795`**; `:798` resolves the path and the re-parse is **`:800`**. Substance fully confirmed, and it is the **third** reader (`jsonl-loaders.ts:210`, `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:800` — grep confirms exactly two file readers plus this one bypass). |\n| 14 | `RetrievalOptions.collections` accepted everywhere, read nowhere; `retrieval-stage.ts:189-197`; the field means collections at some sites, metadata values at others (`corpus-constraint-builder.ts:251-252`) | **CONFIRMED — and worse** | Block is `:189-**198**` (one line longer). The collision is **three-way**, not two: Chroma collection name / manifest metadata value / **corpus folder path** (`icp-api-routes.ts:638`). Unreachability is *structural*, stronger than claimed: no call site anywhere sets `collectionName`/`collectionId` — all 7 constructions are bare `new SmartRetrievalLayer()`. |\n| 15 | `faceted-retrieval.ts` `hybridSearch:324-376` has no rerank path and hardcodes `semanticSearch(q,{maxChunks:20,minRelevance:0.6})` at `:353-356`; 4-arg calls run silently; `tsc --noEmit` reports 157 errors | **PARTIAL — wrong file** | `:324-376` and `:353-356` are in **`smart-retrieval-layer.ts`**, not `faceted-retrieval.ts` (whose `:324-376` is `splitIntoSentences`/`isRelevantToFacet`/`buildSemanticQuery`). Everything else confirmed and worse: it also slices to `DEFAULT_MAX_CHUNKS` = 10 regardless of caller; the 4-arg calls are `faceted-retrieval.ts:154-164`/`:186-195`, reported as `TS2554` at 158,13 and 190,11; error count **exactly 157**. And `minRelevance: 0.6` is not merely hardcoded — it is **inert**, because `semanticSearch` never reads it. |\n| 16 | Live caps: 1 bridge (`cross-author-utils.ts:498`), 3 tensions (`:542`) | **CONFIRMED** | Exact, with the source comments (`// Hard cap at 1 to prevent LLM word salad`). Measured discard: 14 tensions matched, 11 dropped for one topic; 10 matched, 7 dropped for another. |\n| 17 | `cross-author-utils.ts:440-474`/`:500-530` groups by dropping <5-char words, lowercasing, substring containment | **PARTIAL — line ranges wrong** | `:440-448` is the JSDoc; executable code is **`:449-499`** and **`:506-543`**. Substance fully confirmed. **Important asymmetry the claim missed:** the tension side (`:526`) is **one-directional**; the bridge side (`:473-474`) is **bidirectional** — and it is precisely that second direction that produces the `t.includes('')` always-true CRITICAL. |\n| 18 | +0.10 canonical boost applied **after** the cross-encoder (`smart-retrieval-layer.ts:252-291`) | **CONFIRMED** | Rerank at `:239-241`, boost at `:252-291`, re-sort at `:284`. **Additional:** the KG boost at `:583-605`/`:641-642`/`:701` (`×1.2/×1.1/×1.05`, clamped, re-sorted) is a **second** post-rerank override the claim didn't name. Both saturate at 1.0. |\n| 19 | Index-first ordering (\"corpus/index FIRST, ChromaDB fallback\") has ZERO code; live order is inverted | **CONFIRMED** | No ordering/precedence exists on either side. `corpus-index-provider.ts:159` returns three arrays of **pre-rendered markdown strings** with no scores, IDs or provenance — a caller could not order against Chroma results even if it wanted to. On the Python side no path consults `corpus/index` before Chroma. **The index read path is architecturally incapable of being \"first\" as currently typed.** |\n| 20 | `QuotationFidelityValidator` threshold is 0.90 (`quotation-fidelity-stage.ts:60-61`), not 70% | **CONFIRMED (not re-tested this pass)** | The project memory's \"QuotationFidelityValidator (70%+)\" is wrong. More important: the validator compares the draft against the *retrieved chunk*, so the `trimChunkContent` collage means a seam-spanning fabricated quote validates at 100% regardless of threshold. |\n| 21 | `QualityGauntlet` has 10 default stages (`quality-gauntlet.ts:574-589`); comments still say 7 | **CONFIRMED (not re-tested this pass)** | The memory entry \"QualityGauntlet (7 stages)\" is stale. |\n| 22 | `SKIP_DIRS` verbatim at `run_ingest_phase2.py:978`, `run_ingest.py:365`, `parallel_ingest.py:69`; `\"index\"` absent at all three | **CONFIRMED** | `grep -rn SKIP_DIRS scripts/` returns exactly those three, identical five-element sets. |\n| 23 | `should_skip_phase2:312-331` requires `phase >= 2`; 518 of 522 latest index records carry a falsy phase | **CONFIRMED** | Exact. `{None: 518, 5: 4}`, all `status: ok`, extensions `{md:516, txt:2, pdf:4}`. |\n| 24 | `doc_id = sha256(f'{path_rel}:{sha256_file}')[:16]`, chunk ids `{doc_id}:{idx:05d}` at `run_ingest_phase2.py:221-223`, `:659`, `:699` | **CONFIRMED** | And this is the fix for the CRITICAL `undefined:page_start` dedup bug — the unique id already exists and already lands on `chunk.chunkId` at `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:973`. It is simply never used. |\n| 25 | The only delete is `run_ingest_phase2.py:1830` fed by `coll.get(where={\"path_rel\":…})` at `:1686` — returns zero rows once a path changes; no purge script exists | **CONFIRMED (not re-tested this pass)** | |\n| 26 | `god_learn.py:755` defaults `--root` to `<repo>/corpus` | **CONFIRMED** | Verbatim. Since `corpus/index` is a subtree, the default root includes the index. |\n| 27 | `god_learn.py:711-718` `cmd_verify` calls `deduplicate_manifest()` FIRST, 1,182→~696, destroying 248 failed index rows | **REFUTED** | Numbers exact (1182→696, 772→522 index rows, 248 failed removed). But **all 248 have a strictly later `ok` row for the same `path_abs`**; zero current-failure rows are lost; **two failed rows survive**, falsifying the stated consequence; it **prints and logs** the dedup; and the file is git-tracked. This is the handoff's most confidently-wrong item. |\n| 28 | `normalize-edges.py:37-41` hardcodes five `corpus/index/<Entry>/…/global-edges.csv` literals covering none of the five secondary clusters | **CONFIRMED** | Refinement: `KNOWN_PIPELINES` spans **`:36-41`, six entries** — `:36` (`phantasia`) points **outside** `corpus/index`. So `--all` reads six files, five under `corpus/index`. All five secondary clusters have populated `global-edges.csv` and none is registered. |\n| 29 | String-free path-join sites: `endnote-generator.ts:31`, `missing_link_detector.py:439`, `coverage_analyzer.py:470`, `orphan_identifier.py:335` | **PARTIAL** | `missing_link_detector.py:439` and `coverage_analyzer.py:470` are genuine string-free joins. **`orphan_identifier.py:335` is not a path join** — it is an `is_indexed` membership test. **More importantly: none of the three references `corpus/index` at all.** `scripts/common/config.py` defines `corpus_root` (`:49`) and `index_file` (`:52` → `god-learn/index.json`) but has **no `corpus/index` path**. There is no configurable index location anywhere under `scripts/`. |\n| 30 | `.github/workflows/god-audit.yml:5-21` triggers on `corpus/**`, `scripts/ingest/**`, `vector_db_1536/**`; `god-learn-qa.yml:41-53` runs `immutability_checker.py --verify` | **CONFIRMED, with a decisive gap** | `god-audit.yml` paths verified verbatim (also `god-learn/**`, `god-reason/**`, `scripts/audit/**`). **But `grep -rn \"compile-corpus-index\\|compiled-index\" .github/workflows/` returns NOTHING.** No CI job invokes the compiler or asserts anything about the artifact. `god-learn-qa.yml`'s path filters omit `corpus/**` entirely, so an index change never fires it — and its immutability step is already unconditionally red after a fresh checkout (22 of 24 baseline files are untracked → 22 deletion violations → exit 1). |\n\n**Verdict on the existing handoff/implementation plan.** What held up: the compiler's structural facts (parser entry points, `TEXT_DIRS`, Aristotle-only hooks, the tension guard, the no-exit-code posture, the `:718` mechanism, the caching topology, `SKIP_DIRS`, the ingest id scheme, CI triggers). What is wrong and should be struck: the `cmd_verify` manifest-destruction claim (refuted outright), the `normalize-edges` blank-triple claim (wrong metric, unreachable, dead script), the merge idempotence claim (real mechanism, false harm — and it aimed at the wrong file: the actual loss is 1,141 unanchored edges), the `clearJSONLCaches` \"live caller path\" (ESM `require` throws), the `run_ingest.py` skip claim (proposed fix is harmful), and the immutability-checker claim (arithmetic off ~35x, proposed remedy would produce a permanently-red gate). What the handoff **missed entirely and matters most**: the twelve structured `*-ontology.json` files that make the whole scrape-the-markdown architecture unnecessary; the runtime zod rejection of **all 5,437** reasoning edges; the `t.includes('')` always-true bridge matcher; and the `undefined:page_start` de-duplication key.\n\n---\n\n## 3. The data path, end to end\n\n### 3a. An ontology concept — `ψυχή` / \"Soul\"\n\n```\ncorpus/index/Aristotle - Complete Works/de-anima-ontology.md   (source, UTF-8 markdown)\n  │\n  ├─ compile-corpus-index.py:1185   for text_label, cfg in TEXT_DIRS.items()\n  │      ▸ DROP: 8 of 27 content directories never enter this loop (§1b)\n  ├─ :1188/:1193                    is_dir() guards → warn (only warn that can fire)\n  ├─ :1208                          analysis_dir.glob(\"*-ontology.md\")\n  │      ▸ DROP: the 12 sibling *-ontology.json files are never opened\n  ├─ :157-163  read_text()          UTF-8, latin-1 fallback that cannot fail\n  ├─ :1202/:1214 parse_table_ontology(text, text_label)\n  │   ├─ :216-217  if /\\| Field \\| Value \\|/ → reroute whole file (LATENT: 75% node loss)\n  │   ├─ :224-238  slice to \"## Section 3A\", terminator `3[B-Z]` only, magic `start + 10`\n  │   │      ▸ DROP: everything outside 3A, unexamined\n  │   ├─ :244-289  line loop\n  │   │   ├─ :253-256  any non-pipe line resets table state\n  │   │   ├─ :260-261  if len(cells) < 5: continue\n  │   │   │      ▸ DROP: 18 de-anima rows incl. KP1–KP10 with Bekker loci (431a17)\n  │   │   ├─ :264-266  separator skip\n  │   │   ├─ :269-273  header-row detection (empty first cell misfires)\n  │   │   └─ :275-279  first data row consumed as header if no separator\n  │   ├─ :409-427  build hmap — ONLY if len(header_cols) == n exactly\n  │   │      ▸ CORRUPT: one ragged row → positional arm reads Definition column as units\n  │   ├─ :429-506  _parse_table_row\n  │   │   ├─ :430-431  if not name_raw: return None   (silent)\n  │   │   ├─ :166-168  strip_bold — only `**`, so *Umwelt* survives (35 nodes)\n  │   │   ├─ :184-188  parse_units — splits on [,;\\s]+\n  │   │   │      ▸ CORRUPT: 968 tokens become bare English words; '|' 35×\n  │   │   ├─ :477-488  centrality fallback = first letter of cell 0\n  │   │   │      ▸ FABRICATE: 'Phantasia' → 'peripheral'\n  │   │   └─ :495-506  emit {name, greek, transliteration, translation, definition,\n  │   │                      type, units, text, aliases, centralityTier}\n  │   │          ▸ DROP: no id, no source_path, no line, no anchor, no page. PERMANENT.\n  │   └─ (parallel paths: :292 field/value — :308 unbounded split, 94.9% discard;\n  │                       :513 header — :539-540 preamble 37.6% discard, :718 absorb)\n  ├─ :1318-1348  deduplicate_ontology_nodes\n  │      ▸ MERGE: key = name.lower(); 771→701; 51 cross-text collisions\n  │      ▸ DROP: 14,066 chars of definition (longer-string-wins)\n  │      ▸ CORRUPT: `text` concatenated, tier/type NOT merged (first TEXT_DIRS entry wins)\n  ├─ :1276-1304  build_canonical_terms  → 1,722 strings, 101 nondeterministic ties\n  └─ :1374-1387  json.dump(indent=2) → corpus/index/compiled-index.json   [664,494 B]\n         ▸ NONDETERMINISM: builtAt (:1375) + term order (:1304)\n         ▸ NO atomic write, NO minimum-count guard, NO backup, EXIT 0 unconditionally\n\n── artifact boundary ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n  ├─ jsonl-loaders.ts:200   resolve(root,'corpus','index','compiled-index.json')\n  ├─ :205-207               mtime cache (float ms only; no size, no hash)\n  ├─ :210-211               readFileSync + JSON.parse  → `any`\n  │      ▸ NO Zod, NO shape check, despite the docstring at :6\n  ├─ :215-217               } catch { return null; }   ← total blackout, zero logs\n  │\n  ├─ corpus-index-provider.ts:106-109  terms = topic.split(/\\W+/).filter(len>=4)\n  │      ▸ DROP: 'soul','body','mind','nous' — the four-letter vocabulary\n  ├─ :81-91   scoreCandidate — raw substring count, global regex, no boundary, no norm\n  │      ▸ RANK: dominated by definition length\n  ├─ :118     .filter(score>0).sort().slice(0, 12)\n  │      ▸ DROP: 55 of 67 scoring nodes, no count, no log; ties → JSON array order\n  ├─ :120-127 render\n  │      ▸ DROP: translation, type, text, aliases, centralityTier never rendered\n  │      ▸ DROP: definition.slice(0,200)   — 37.2% of all definition text\n  │      ▸ DROP: units.slice(0,5)          — 2,259 of 4,059 references\n  └─ retrieval-stage.ts:470-477 → gold-standard-prompt-builder → PROMPT TOKEN\n```\n\n**Terminus:** the model receives `- **ψυχή** (psyche): <≤200 chars> [DA-02, META-01, META-01-10, META-02, META-03]` — **no work, no page, no Bekker locus, no build id**. Measured total index content reaching a prompt on a well-matched topic: **5,271 of 656,755 chars = 0.803%**.\n\n### 3b. A unit record — `META-07`\n\n```\ncorpus/index/Aristotle - Complete Works/units/aristotle-meta-07.json\n  { \"unit_id\": \"META-07\",\n    \"bekker_range\": \"1042a–1052a\",\n    \"pdf_pages\": \"65–75\",\n    \"pdf_file\": \"Aristotle - Metaphysics_(2014)_[My Copy].pdf\" }\n```\n\n**This is exactly the provenance the goal requires, and it already exists on disk.**\n\n```\n  ├─ compile-corpus-index.py:1208 globs \"*-ontology.md\" ONLY\n  │      ▸▸ TERMINATES HERE. No unit record is ever opened by the compiler.\n  │\n  └─ The only trace of META-07 anywhere downstream is the bare string token\n     \"META-07\" inside node.units, produced by parse_units (:184-188) from an\n     ontology-markdown cell.\n        ├─ 1,669 of 4,059 tokens are prose garbage that resolve to nothing\n        ├─ corpus-index-provider.ts:125  units.slice(0,5)  →  META-07 dropped\n        └─ grep -rn \"bekker_range\\|unit_id\\|pdf_pages\\|pdf_file\" --include=*.ts src/\n              → NO OUTPUT.\n```\n\n**Terminus:** the join is never performed, in either language. The registry's `bekker_range`/`pdf_pages`/`pdf_file` — the citation anchors — are unreachable from runtime by any code path. Granularity delivered is book/section-level: **3–4 orders of magnitude coarser than clause-level.**\n\n### 3c. Edges — three journeys, three dead ends\n\n**(i) Tension edges** — `corpus/index/<Entry>/<analysis>/tension-edges.json`\n```\n:1258-1268 collect_tension_edges — one filename literal, TEXT_DIRS-gated\n   ▸ DROP: 12 of 19 entries have no file; 8 more dirs unregistered; NO warn (no else at :1268)\n:1097-1101 unwrap \"tensions\" key\n:1120-1129 _normalize_tension_edge — requires node_a/node_b\n   ▸ DROP: 55 of 119 records (Burke 16, Calleja 12, Gross 15, Wendt 12) → 64 survive\n:1165-1174 8-field projection\n   ▸ DROP: 13 keys / 3,698 B — locus_a, locus_b, provenance, interp_level, title,\n           contributors, works, chapters, status, node_c (triadic → binary)\n   ▸ CORRUPT: :1148-1152 writes one value into BOTH dependency and conflict (10 Uexküll edges)\n   ▸ ids per-file, unnamespaced → 32 of 64 collide\ncross-author-utils.ts:506-543 getActiveTensions\n   ▸ :516-518 words <5 dropped; :525 searchText EXCLUDES dependencyRelation/conflictRelation\n   ▸ :542 slice(0,3) — 11 of 14 matches discarded\ncorpus-index-provider.ts:148-156 render → PROMPT (as prose, without the disagreement)\n```\n**Terminus:** 64 of 119 records arrive as prose pairs. **52 of 64 reference no ontology node at either end** — it is not a graph and cannot be traversed.\n\n**(ii) CSV edges** — 240 files, **20,610 rows**, the densest curated content in the index\n```\nrun_ingest_phase2.py:197 ALLOWED_EXTS  →  .csv EXCLUDED\n   ▸▸ no ingest path exists.\nnormalize-edges.py:35-42 KNOWN_PIPELINES  →  6 files, 792 deduped rows (3.8%)\n   ├─ :129 relation passed through with .strip()  (633 distinct values, unnormalized)\n   ├─ :135-144 8-field schema  →  locus dropped for the 110-file majority header\n   ├─ :150-156 restkey filtered → 29 rows lose their entire annotation\n   └─ :286-291 stdout only, unless --output\n   ▸ ZERO callers repo-wide; file is UNTRACKED in git.\n```\n**Terminus: 234 of 240 CSVs have no code path to runtime at all.** 0% of curated edge loci reach a prompt.\n\n**(iii) Reasoning edges**\n```\nreason_over_knowledge.py:286-370 O(n²) → :449-457 write god-reason/reasoning.jsonl (5,437)\n   ▸ TRUNCATES the file; merge-reasoning-edges.py writes the same path (:19 == :22)\n   ▸ ~half of asymmetric directions reversed (:130-146 vs :319)\nmerge-reasoning-edges.py:66-76 anchor → 1 concept per claim; 218/1,463 terms unmatchable\n   ▸ 16.7% → unanchored-edges.jsonl (803 records) — READ BY NOTHING\njsonl-loaders.ts:78-107 loadReasoningEdgesSync → types.ts:58-62 zod\n   ▸▸ source/target required, Phase 7 emits neither.\n   ▸▸ PASS: 0   DROPPED: 5437.\n```\n**Terminus: the schema.** Every consumer sees `[]`. The reasoning layer is dead at runtime.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Silent-failure inventory\n\n*Every place content is discarded, an error swallowed, or wrong output produced without saying so. Grouped by mechanism.*\n\n### A. Discards with no warning, no counter, no exit code — compiler (23 in-branch sites)\n\n| path:line | Discarded | Measured today |\n|---|---|---|\n| `:260-261` | table rows <5 cells | 18 de-anima rows, incl. KP1–KP10 with Bekker loci |\n| `:216-217` | entire file rerouted on one `\\| Field \\| Value \\|` line | latent; would destroy 177 of 236 nodes |\n| `:224-238` | everything outside the `## 3A` slice | whole-file for non-3A layouts |\n| `:253-256` | table state reset on any non-pipe line → next row eaten at `:611-614` | latent, one blank line away |\n| `:269-273` | data row with empty first cell misread as header | latent |\n| `:275-279` | first data row consumed as header when separator missing | whole table → 0 nodes |\n| `:308-321` | last `### N` section absorbs to EOF, 94.9% then discarded | 9,867 + 3,431 chars; 14 Key Positions with loci |\n| `:310` | `sections[0]` preamble | physics \"Targeted Concepts List\" |\n| `:327-328`, `:346-347` | section with no pipe table → `None` | silent; header proves intent |\n| `:338`, `:343` | cells <2; unrecognised field keys | **3,099 chars (12.6%)**, incl. **all 26 `global_candidate`** flags |\n| `:344` | last-wins field overwrite, no collision detection | latent tier substitution |\n| `:361`, `:365` | parentheticals stripped from greek/transliteration | `(τὸ) ὄν` → `ὄν` |\n| `:430-431` | row with no name | silent |\n| `:456-474` | positional column guesswork | `type` = translation, units from prose |\n| `:539-540` | preamble before first node marker | **182,218 of 484,809 B (37.6%)** |\n| `:569-570` | header file with no `\\|` in the 3A window | HR, Uexküll tables |\n| `:588-592`, `:611-614` | blank line inside table deletes the next row | verified `['Alpha','Gamma']` |\n| `:596-597` | rows <4 cells (different threshold from `:260`, undocumented) | |\n| `:605-609` | first cell containing \"node\" eats the row **and** corrupts `header_cols` | verified node named `'8'` |\n| `:649-651`, `:689-691`, `:727-728` | whole node → `None` | 0 today, nothing would report a change |\n| `:661`, `:666`, `:667`, `:672` | `First Unit`, transliteration, translation, aliases hardcoded empty | |\n| `:714-717` | empty field key → value dropped, accumulator left falsy | |\n| `:718-719` | 108 lines / 21,879 chars absorbed into open fields | 2 corrupt shipped nodes |\n| `:756-767` | every non-schema field key parsed then dropped | 7 keys live, incl. all of Rickert's T1 tension structure — **732 bytes parsed and thrown away in the same call** |\n| `:827`, `:837` | hook sections under 100/80 chars — undocumented magic numbers | 0 today |\n| `:1015-1025` | `first_sentence` on bridge/relevance | **23,843 of 33,975 chars (70.2%)**; 66/72 empty relevance |\n| `:1110`, `:1128-1129` | tension records without `node_a`/`node_b` | **55 of 119** |\n| `:1165-1174` | 13 tension keys incl. all page loci | 3,698 B |\n| `:1188`, `:1205`, `:1229`, `:1241` | missing dirs/files — these **do** warn, to a stderr nobody reads | |\n| `:1268` | missing `tension-edges.json` — **no else branch at all** | 12 of 19 entries |\n| `:1290`, `:1300` | 1-char lemmas; 1-2 char translations | 13 terms unreachable incl. `ὕλη`, `ἁφή`, `φῶς` |\n| `:1319-1348` | 70 nodes absorbed, 14,066 chars of definition | no per-merge log |\n| `:1383-1387` | overwrites the tracked artifact with no guard | exit 0 even if all arrays empty |\n\n### B. Errors caught and discarded\n\n| path:line | Swallowed | Observable |\n|---|---|---|\n| `jsonl-loaders.ts:215-217` | `} catch { return null; }` over stat+read+parse | **nothing** — total index blackout is indistinguishable from a short topic |\n| `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:290` | `} catch { /* non-fatal */ }` around the whole canonical-boost block | nothing |\n| `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:131-176` | Chroma resolution failure latches, `semanticSearch` returns `[]` not throws | the documented F-13 breaker at `:306` never receives anything |\n| `quality-integration.ts:749-764` | ESM `require` throws `ReferenceError` **on every call**, caught by `catch { /* non-fatal */ }` | `detectUnanchoredEdges` runs with `ontologyExpansion` permanently empty — **always-on silent degradation, zero output** |\n| `reason_over_knowledge.py:203-212` | bare `except Exception: pass` over the index load, result cached for process lifetime | corrupt index ≡ index with no hooks |\n| `god_learn.py:56-64` | malformed reasoning lines `continue` | `total_edges` undercounts; corrupt file passes the gate as clean |\n| `god_learn.py:389-408` | JSON decode errors while rebuilding `index.json` offsets | prints `N` KUs / `M` offsets with `N != M` unflagged — and it's an **autofix** |\n| `god_learn.py:263-270`, `:289-300`, `:164-166` | three bare `except Exception`; `switch_gpu_mode`'s `False` ignored by all 4 callers | \"GPU mode switch failed\" becomes a confusing downstream embedding error |\n| `merge-reasoning-edges.py:92-93` | no `exists()` guard on `BACKUP_EDGES` (the human-curated ground truth, in `tmp/`) | `FileNotFoundError` with no context |\n| `compile-corpus-index.py:282-287`, `:314-319` | two `try/except` + `warn` blocks that **cannot execute** — neither callee can raise | the docstring's promised diagnostic path does not exist |\n\n### C. Wrong output produced confidently\n\n| path:line | Wrong thing | Detectability |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cross-author-utils.ts:474` → `:498` → `gold-standard-prompt-builder.ts:712-716` | prompt asserts a MANDATORY bridge to an author named **\"Unknown\"** with an empty bridge | none — reads as a normal instruction |\n| `cross-author-utils.ts:342` (stale flag) | prompt renders literal **`(undefined)`** | none; `:364` has already logged \"Bridge activated\" |\n| `cross-author-utils.ts:317` | 71 of 117 primary texts labelled **SECONDARY SCHOLARSHIP** | none |\n| `retrieval-utils.ts:352-370` | non-contiguous sentence **collage** presented as continuous source prose | none — fidelity validator compares against the collage |\n| `retrieval-stage.ts:226` | de-dup by page number across all authors | none |\n| `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:958-970` | missing `distances` → **every chunk scores 1.0** | presents as maximally confident retrieval |\n| `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:194` | `collections` ignored → `findCrossReferences` reports De Anima \"agrees\" with Being and Time using a third author's chunk | logs claim scoping happened |\n| `retrieval-stage.ts:189-198` | **logs** `Textual analysis collections added: …` and queries the same collection | the log asserts what did not happen |\n| `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:1186-1199` | reranker unreachable → one warn per process, then silence; log still says \"after rerank: 30\" | one line, once |\n| `cross-author-utils.ts:577-578` | `information`/`transformation` inject `εἶδος` into the embedding query | none |\n| `compile-corpus-index.py:718` | `Temporalität` ships tension T8's units as its own — **syntactically valid, wholly wrong provenance** | none; source says `Intro-U2, D2-U6` |\n| `compile-corpus-index.py:350` | node named `Contradiction (PNC)`; the true name exists nowhere | none |\n| `compile-corpus-index.py:1067-1070` | metaphysics hooks labelled `targetText: 'Physics'` — self-loops | none |\n| `compile-corpus-index.py:1148-1152` | 10 Uexküll edges assert a fabricated dependency==conflict symmetry | none |\n| `compile-corpus-index.py:481-486` | `'Phantasia'` → tier `peripheral` by first letter | indistinguishable from parsed values |\n| `reason_over_knowledge.py:130-146`, `:319` | ~half of asymmetric edge directions reversed; `\"by means of\"` → `defined_as` | none |\n| `corpus-constraint-builder.ts:295-324` | `(Barrett 471)` on a 300-page book → **valid** | none |\n| `corpus-constraint-builder.ts:110-121` | a real corpus work excluded from the whitelist → its correct citation flagged hallucinated | inverted signal |\n| `retrieval-stage.ts:241-465` vs `stage-types.ts:63-66` | a run where **every** sub-query failed reports `pipelineHealth: 'clean'` | none |\n| `god_learn.py:648-661` | reports \"no contradictions\" over 5,437 edges it structurally cannot check | reads as a pass |\n\n### D. Diagnostics on the wrong stream or never wired\n`compile-corpus-index.py:1356` — the one diagnostic that fires on the live corpus is a bare `print()` to **stdout**, formatted to look like a `warn()`. `2>/dev/null` shows it; `1>/dev/null` hides it. Any wrapper grepping stderr for `WARNING` sees a clean build.\n`scripts/verify-hardening.ts` — the only executable check over the read path, in neither CI nor `package.json`, passing by luck on a hand-picked query.\n`.github/workflows/` — **zero references to `compile-corpus-index` or `compiled-index`**; `god-learn-qa.yml`'s path filters omit `corpus/**`; its immutability step is already unconditionally red (22 of 24 baseline files untracked).\n\n---\n\n## 5. State, caching, and determinism\n\n### 5a. Module-level caches and globals\n\n| # | Location | Key | Invalidation | Goes stale when | What silently degrades | Reset exists? |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `jsonl-loaders.ts:191` `_compiledIndexCache` | `{path, mtimeMs}` | mtime + path | sub-ms rewrite; `cp -p`; container layer restore; symlink retarget | serves stale index indefinitely | `clearJSONLCaches():305` — **unreachable (ESM `require`)** |\n| 2 | `cross-author-utils.ts:56` `_hooksDerivationDone` | *none* — one-shot boolean | **NONE** | any recompile; any `projectRoot` change; any cache clear | **CRITICAL:** `sourceAuthor`/`targetAuthor` → `undefined`; ICP cross-author backfill dies at `icp-orchestrator.ts:368` after logging success; prompt renders `(undefined)` | **NO — grep returns exactly 3 lines** |\n| 3 | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:795` `this.protectedTerms` | *none* | **NONE** | recompile adds terms | new ontology terms stripped as stopwords for process lifetime; inconsistent view of one file within one process | no |\n| 4 | `jsonl-loaders.ts:224` `_authorKUIndexCache` | `mtimeMs` **only — `path` omitted** | mtime | two roots share an mtime | cross-project contamination of author-scoped KU lookups | via `clearJSONLCaches` (unreachable) |\n| 5 | `jsonl-loaders.ts:49`, `:258`, `:281` | `{path,mtimeMs}` | mtime | as #1 | — | via `clearJSONLCaches` (unreachable) |\n| 6 | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:1430` retrieval LRU | query+opts hash | 30 min TTL, 1,000 entries, **O(n) eviction** | mid-TTL corpus re-ingest | **CRITICAL:** caller mutates the cached objects in place (`retrieval-stage.ts:305/:319/:346`) → cache holds trimmed collages, not corpus text. Also caches `[]` on infra failure. | no corpus coupling at all |\n| 7 | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:143` `COLLECTION_ID` / `collectionResolved` | one-shot latch | **NONE** | Chroma unavailable at first use | retrieval permanently disabled for the process, `[]` returned not thrown | no |\n| 8 | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:70` `rerankWarned` | static one-shot | **NONE** | reranker unreachable | one warn, then permanently unreranked while logs report rerank | no |\n| 9 | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:60-61` `kgKUs` / `kgEdges` | in-memory arrays | — | — | fully resident: 588 KUs + 5,437 edges today | no |\n| 10 | `reason_over_knowledge.py:190` `_hook_licensed_pairs` | one-shot global, **relative path** | **NONE** | wrong CWD; index recompiled mid-process; index corrupt | all hook-licensed cross-author edges silently disabled; failure ≡ \"no hooks\" | no |\n\n**Two entangled design decisions.** Caches #1 and #5 hand out the **live object by reference**, unfrozen — and `cross-author-utils.ts:345` *intentionally mutates* it. So the cache doubles as mutable shared state across three modules, and freezing cannot land until the derivation is moved into the loader.\n\n**Three readers, one file.** `grep -rn 'compiled-index.json' src/` → `jsonl-loaders.ts:200`, `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:798`. The third path (`corpus-index-provider.ts`) delegates but **advertises an `indexPath` parameter it silently ignores** (`:73-77`, `:200-202`), so a pinned-snapshot session reads the live index instead. The loader's own docstring (`:195-196`) says the others \"should delegate instead of maintaining their own caches\"; `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:800` does not.\n\n### 5b. Sources of nondeterminism in `compiled-index.json`\n\n| Source | path:line | Magnitude | Fix |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `builtAt` wall-clock stamp, microsecond precision, unconditional | `:1375` | guarantees a diff on every run; the field is **read by nothing** (`corpus-index-provider.ts:53` declares it, no consumer) | drop or content-hash — 3 lines |\n| `canonicalTerms` from a `set`, sorted on `(-len, t.lower())` with 101 exact ties | `:1283`, `:1304` | 5 processes → 5 digests; fresh compile differs from shipped in **106 of 1,722 positions** | add `t` as final key — 1 line |\n| Node array order → cap-boundary selection | `:1319-1348` → `corpus-index-provider.ts:118` | 37 candidates tie at the cutoff with no secondary key; V8's stable sort means **which 12 of 44 nodes reach the prompt is fixed by JSON array index**, which dedup reshuffles between builds | secondary key — 3 lines |\n| Node array order → anchor identity | `merge-reasoning-edges.py:52-62` | lookup keyed case-sensitively, matched case-insensitively, 1,448 length ties; recompiling can flip a claim's anchor `Soul`↔`ψυχή`, `Being`↔`οὐσία` — changing edge identity graph-wide with **no diff signal** | key on `.lower()`, total sort, resolve 15 collisions |\n| `TEXT_DIRS` dict-literal order → merge winner | `:35-133` → `:1344-1346` | `type`/`centralityTier` never merged; the first entry wins; Part III clusters are listed **first**, so they systematically demote primary sources | rank tiers, keep max |\n\n**Net:** two runs on unchanged input produce different files. `git diff` on the tracked artifact is pure noise — the current diff is 583 insertions / 55 deletions in one file, and **no reviewer can separate a real content change from seed churn.** Reproducing a drafting session's inputs is impossible, and the one field that could record which build a draft came from is dead.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Coupling and blast radius\n\n### 6a. Relocating `corpus/index` — the true must-change list\n\n**Literal-string sites (a grep for `corpus/index` finds these) — 12 live code sites:**\n\n| path:line | Form |\n|---|---|\n| `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:5` | docstring |\n| `scripts/normalize-edges.py:37` | `\"corpus/index/Rickert - Ambient Rhetoric/rickert-analysis/global-edges.csv\"` |\n| `scripts/normalize-edges.py:38` | `\"corpus/index/Heidegger - Being and Time/bt-analysis/global-edges.csv\"` |\n| `scripts/normalize-edges.py:39` | `\"corpus/index/Heidegger - Basic Concepts of Aristotelian Philosophy/bcap-analysis/global-edges.csv\"` |\n| `scripts/normalize-edges.py:40` | `\"corpus/index/Von Uexkull - A Foray into the Worlds of Animals and Humans/uex-analysis/global-edges.csv\"` |\n| `scripts/normalize-edges.py:41` | `\"corpus/index/Aristotle - Complete Works/global-edges.csv\"` |\n| `scripts/merge-reasoning-edges.py:7` | docstring |\n| `scripts/reason/reason_over_knowledge.py:199` | `Path(\"corpus/index/compiled-index.json\")` — **relative, CWD-dependent** |\n| `src/god-agent/shared/jsonl-loaders.ts:200` | `resolve(root,'corpus','index','compiled-index.json')` |\n| `src/god-agent/shared/cross-author-utils.ts:10` | docstring |\n| `src/god-agent/retrieval/smart-retrieval-layer.ts:798` | `resolve(process.cwd(),'corpus','index','compiled-index.json')` — **CWD-dependent** |\n| `src/god-agent/universal/write-pipeline-orchestrator.ts:1772, :3430, :4030` | comments |\n\n**String-free sites — these survive any grep-driven migration:**\n\n| path:line | Construction |\n|---|---|\n| `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:31` | `CORPUS_INDEX = REPO / \"corpus\" / \"index\"` |\n| `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py:32` | `OUTPUT = CORPUS_INDEX / \"compiled-index.json\"` |\n| `scripts/merge-reasoning-edges.py:21` | `COMPILED_INDEX = REPO / \"corpus\" / \"index\" / \"compiled-index.json\"` |\n| `tests/data-integrity/test_reasoning_edges.py:18` | `COMPILED_INDEX = REPO / \"corpus\" / \"index\" / \"compiled-index.json\"` |\n| `scripts/god_learn/god_learn.py:755` | `--root` default `str(rr / \"corpus\")` — **includes `corpus/index` transitively** |\n| `scripts/audit/core/missing_link_detector.py:187, :439` | `PROJECT_ROOT / \"corpus\"` (+ `/ path_rel`) |\n| `scripts/audit/core/coverage_analyzer.py:470` | `PROJECT_ROOT / \"corpus\" / document_path` |\n| `scripts/audit/core/orphan_identifier.py:295` | `PROJECT_ROOT / \"corpus\"` |\n| `scripts/audit/core/provenance_tracer.py:153` | `self.project_root / \"corpus\"` |\n| `scripts/dashboard/app.py:43` | `CORPUS_DIR = PROJECT_ROOT / \"corpus\"` |\n| `scripts/common/config.py:49` | `\"corpus_root\": str(PROJECT_ROOT / \"corpus\")` — **defines `corpus_root` and `index_file` (→`god-learn/index.json`) but has NO `corpus/index` entry** |\n| `scripts/growth/core/{corpus_version_manager.py:164, document_tracker.py:70, density_analyzer.py:124}`, `scripts/growth/cli/growth_cli.py:73, :370` | `base_path / \"corpus\"` |\n\n**Corrections to the prior handoff:** `orphan_identifier.py:335` is **not** a path join (it is an `is_indexed` membership test — the real site is `:295`). More importantly, **none of the three previously-cited \"string-free\" sites references `corpus/index` at all**; they reference `corpus/`. There is **no configurable `corpus/index` location anywhere under `scripts/`** — the six sites above *are* the complete configuration surface, and four of them are module-level constants.\n\n**Two hardcoded absolute paths / CWD dependencies that break silently on relocation:**\n- `reason_over_knowledge.py:199` — bare relative `Path`; wrong CWD → `exists()` False → empty licensed-pair set → **all hook-licensed edges silently disabled, no log** (`:203-212` swallows).\n- `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:798` — `process.cwd()`; wrong CWD → `existsSync` false → **empty protected-term set, cached for process lifetime, no log**.\n- `god_learn.py:273-286`, `:535` — hardcoded `Path(\"/tmp\")` and `/tmp/phase4_hits.json`, ignoring `TMPDIR`; two concurrent runs cross-contaminate the promotion input (`:591` checks only existence and size).\n- `merge-reasoning-edges.py:18` — `REPO/'tmp'/'backup-pre-ku-plan-2026-03-18'/'data'/'reasoning.jsonl'`, the **only** input with no `exists()` guard, holding the human-curated ground truth in a scratch directory.\n\n**Also required for relocation:** `SKIP_DIRS` at `run_ingest_phase2.py:978`, `run_ingest.py:365`, `parallel_ingest.py:69` — three identical literal sets that must gain the new directory name (they lack `\"index\"` today).\n\n### 6b. Renaming any single entry directory — must-change list\n\n| path:line | What breaks |\n|---|---|\n| `compile-corpus-index.py:35-133` | The `TEXT_DIRS` key **is** the directory name. Rename → `:1188` warns \"Directory not found\" to a stderr nobody reads → that entry's nodes vanish → summary at `:1391` shows a smaller number, indistinguishable from success. |\n| `compile-corpus-index.py:1239` | `\"Aristotle - Complete Works\"` literal — renaming Aristotle silently zeroes **all 72 hooks**. |\n| `normalize-edges.py:36-41` | Five full-path literals; rename → `[SKIP]` line, exit 0. |\n| `normalize-edges.py:45-56` | `PATH_HINTS` substring tuples for auto-detection. |\n| `compile-corpus-index.py:145-151` `ARISTOTLE_WORK_MAP` | filename-stem→label map. |\n| `corpus/index/**/_synthesis/manifest.json` (22 files) | cross-references entries by directory path (e.g. `\"path\": \"corpus/index/Virtual Learning Environments (King–Salvo)/\"`). |\n| `compiled-index.json` itself | `node.text` and `tensionEdge.text` carry the label; 51 nodes have semicolon-joined composites. No migration path — the artifact must be rebuilt, which changes 106 canonicalTerm positions and `builtAt` as collateral. |\n\nThere is **no** single directory-name constant. The name is duplicated across a Python dict literal, five path strings, a hint tuple list, 22 JSON manifests, and the artifact's own data. **The rename failure mode is total silence with exit 0 at every one of them.**\n\n### 6c. CI triggers\n\n| Workflow | Path filters (`:5-21` / `:41-53`) | Fires on a `corpus/index` change? | Actually checks the index? |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `.github/workflows/god-audit.yml` | `god-learn/**`, `god-reason/**`, `corpus/**`, `scripts/audit/**`, `scripts/ingest/**`, `vector_db_1536/**` (push + PR to main, + `workflow_dispatch`) | **YES** — `corpus/**` matches | **NO** — `grep` for `compile-corpus-index\\|compiled-index` across `.github/workflows/` returns **nothing** |\n| `.github/workflows/god-learn-qa.yml` | `god-learn/**`, `god-reason/**`, `scripts/learn/**`, `scripts/reason/**`, `scripts/qa/**`, `qa/baselines/**` | **NO** — `corpus/**` absent | its `immutability_checker.py --verify` step is already unconditionally red after a fresh checkout (22 of 24 baseline files untracked → 22 deletion violations → exit 1) |\n\n**Net: no CI job invokes the compiler or asserts anything about the artifact.** The single test that touches it (`tests/data-integrity/test_reasoning_edges.py:73-78`) is tautological *and* unwired (`grep` for `pytest`/`tests` in workflows: no match). The 10,009-char `centralityTier` has been shipped since `builtAt 2026-07-20T16:03:58Z` and survived three subsequent feature commits, because nothing asserts that a centrality tier is one of three words.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Scalability ceiling — the section that decides the programme\n\n**Target:** claim-level and clause-level records for every document. Sizing from the actual corpus: 224 ingested documents × ~200 claims ≈ **45,000 claim records**; × ~10 clauses ≈ **450,000 clause records**. At the stated 100x that is ~4.5M claims / ~45M clauses. At the measured 712 bytes/record that is **~32 MB** at claim level today and **~320 MB** at clause level; at 100x, ~22 GB.\n\n### Component-by-component breaking points\n\n| Component | Breaks at | Why — with the number |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Compiler** (`compile-corpus-index.py`) | **Already broken. 1x.** | Runtime is not the constraint (48 files, <1 s; 100x is still seconds). What breaks is **silence**: 0 warnings while discarding 37.6% of header source, 70.2% of hook prose, 55 of 119 tensions, 70 nodes. At 100x that is ~200 silently corrupt nodes and ~18 MB of silently discarded source, with exit 0 every time. **Registration** is a 19-key hand-maintained literal that has already lost 8 of 27 directories; at 100x it needs ~1,900 hand-written entries. And the emitted schema has **no slot for provenance** — the parsers work on `text.splitlines()` and `re.split()` and discard offsets in the first statement of every function (`:244`, `:326`, `:533`, `:577`, `:679`, `:701`), so there is no point in the code where a byte offset is still available. |\n| **Artifact format** (single pretty-printed JSON) | **~30–50 MB, i.e. ~50x.** | 664,494 B for 701 nodes = 712 B/record; `indent=2` alone costs 137,323 B (20.7%). Node parses it in 3.8 ms for **5.7 MB heap — 8.6× expansion** — and does so twice per process. 320 MB of clause-level JSON ⇒ ~2.8 GB heap per parse, ~1.8 s of blocked event loop, twice. V8's `MAX_STRING_LENGTH` (536,870,888) is a hard wall on `readFileSync('utf-8')` regardless of RAM. And it is **git-tracked and rewritten in full on every build**, with `builtAt` + 202 hash-ordered positions guaranteeing a diff even for a no-op — a 32 MB churning tracked file makes the repository unreviewable. |\n| **Loader** (`jsonl-loaders.ts:89`, `:210`) | **24.97x — not 100x.** | `reasoning.jsonl` is 21,498,945 B today. `readFileSync` into one JS string throws `ERR_STRING_TOO_LONG` at 536,870,888 chars. Two different undiagnosable failures from one cause: `:89` throws **uncaught** (process death); `:210` is inside the bare catch → **silent total blackout**. `raw.split('\\n')` doubles peak memory and blocks the event loop 150 ms today → 3.75 s at 25x, synchronously, inside daemons. |\n| **Cache layer** | **Already degrading at 1x; no ceiling because it never grows.** | 30-min TTL LRU, 1,000 entries, **O(n) eviction per insert at capacity**, each entry up to 28 chunk bodies (~84 MB at 3 KB/chunk). **Nothing invalidates on re-ingest.** The mutation-through-cache defect means it caches derivatives, not the corpus. `_hooksDerivationDone` and `protectedTerms` never invalidate at all. At claim level, cache entries become claim sets and the entry-count cap becomes meaningless. |\n| **Retrieval path** | **Pool cap 50 — a hard constant, at any volume.** | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:926` caps the candidate pool at `Math.min(maxChunks*3, 50)`; no configuration exceeds it (perversely, rerank OFF gives `maxChunks*2` = up to 80, so enabling the reranker *narrows* the pool). The KG boost is a pure linear scan: today `5,437 + |topicConcepts|×5,437 + |expansionConcepts|×5,437` ≈ **1.2M iterations per sub-query**, ×8–15 sub-queries. At 100x (58,800 KUs, 543,700 edges) that is **~120M iterations per sub-query** — tens of seconds of single-threaded JS each — with both arrays fully resident. Canonical-boost is O(1,722) substring tests per query → ~170,000 at 100x. The `undefined:page_start` de-dup key **gets worse with volume** because more works share low page numbers. |\n| **Prompt builder** | **Two opposite walls.** | `corpus-index-provider.ts:101-103` caps are **absolute integers**, so at 100x the emitted context is byte-identical while the discard rate goes **82% → 99.8%** — the system does not get slower, it gets proportionally blinder, silently. Conversely `buildCorpusCatalog` (`cross-author-utils.ts:307-331`) is the **one** component that scales linearly: 8,439 chars / ~2,110 tokens today → **~844 KB / ~211,000 tokens at 100x**, injected uncapped into every decomposition prompt. Hard wall at **~90x**, with quality degradation well before. |\n| **Reasoner** (`reason_over_knowledge.py`) | **Already at 86% of budget.** | 588 KUs → 25,334 intra + 147,244 cross = **172,578 pairs against a 200,000 default**. One more corpus entry and the cross-author pass at `:349` silently never runs — it only `break`s. At 100x, 1.73 billion pairs. `char_ngrams` recomputed inside the inner loop: 345,156 calls for 588 distinct claims. Anchoring is ~289 s today → **~80 h at 100x**, single-threaded, with no incremental mode. |\n| **Manifest / ingest** | **Superlinear in the wrong direction.** | `deduplicate_manifest` reads the whole 1.08 MB file into memory and rewrites it non-atomically → ~100 MB read-modify-write at 100x. And because `SKIP_DIRS` lacks `\"index\"` and 518/522 index records carry a falsy `phase`, **all 516 index markdown files are re-chunked and re-embedded on every compile** — the index gets more expensive to ingest the more index there is. |\n\n### Recommendation: **REPLACE the parse-and-emit layer. HARDEN the loaders, the orchestration, and the reasoner's skeleton.**\n\nI am not hedging: the split is the answer, and each half is argued below.\n\n**REPLACE — `compile-corpus-index.py`'s parse and emit layers (~1,100 of 1,412 lines), `normalize-edges.py` (306 lines, entire), `merge-reasoning-edges.py` (237 lines, entire), and the TS matching/rendering layer (`cross-author-utils.ts:408-614` + `corpus-index-provider.ts:79-197`, ~600 lines).**\n\nFour pieces of evidence, in order of force.\n\n1. **The structured data already exists and the compiler ignores it.** `grep -c \"ontology.json\"` over 1,412 lines returns **0**, while **12 `*-ontology.json` files sit in the same directories the compiler scrapes**. *Heidegger and Rhetoric*'s is 56,912 bytes with structured `canonical_nodes` carrying `contributors` and `cross_pipeline_links`, `contested_concepts` with per-contributor readings, and a `tension_summary` — precisely the fields the markdown scrape loses. **The pipeline is doing the hardest possible job — recovering structure from prose — when the structure is on disk in the same folder.** Hardening a scraper that competes with a structured twin is work spent to reach a worse result. This single fact decides the harden-or-replace question.\n\n2. **The defect density is architectural, not incidental.** In one 500-line window: 2 corrupt shipped nodes, 17+ silent-discard branches, 4 dead/unreachable blocks, 3 latent silent-row-deletion paths, zero tests. The bugs are not independent — they descend from one decision, to parse a structured document with line-at-a-time regex and mutable flags. The *same* unbounded-section bug exists independently in **two** parsers (`:308` and `:718`), which is what happens when three markdown dialects get three hand-rolled scanners instead of one grammar. Fixing `:718` fixes 2 nodes; it does not make `:539-540`, `:558`, `:606`, `:611-614` or the absent provenance any less true.\n\n3. **The schema is a dead end for the stated goal, and that is not tunable.** A claim record is `(text, source_path, heading_path, line_start, line_end, char_start, char_end, type, subject, polarity, evidence_refs)`. The emitted dict has ten flat fields and **not one is an identity or an anchor**. Adding provenance is not a schema addition — it requires the parsers to track offsets, which none of them do, at any point. Meanwhile the corpus already *contains* claim-level records: `metaphysics-ontology.md` `## 3. Key Positions` is 14 numbered claims each with a Bekker locus and a status, and this code absorbs all fourteen into the ὄρεξις node's `fields` dict as keys `'1'..'14'` and drops them at `:379-390`. **The data exists; the schema has nowhere to put it.** Likewise the compiler demonstrably parses Rickert's tension structure (`node a`, `node b`, `dependency edge`, `conflict edge`, `synthesis`) and then throws 732 bytes away in the same function call, because the return dict has no slot.\n\n4. **Nothing depends on current behaviour, so the replacement cost ≈ the hardening cost.** `grep -rln` over `tests/` finds **zero** tests referencing any of the three TS modules; the sole check is `scripts/verify-hardening.ts`, in neither CI nor `package.json`, whose one bridge assertion passes only because its query happens to contain a literal German word sitting in a `targetConcept`. And the always-true `t.includes('')` at `cross-author-utils.ts:474` means **the bridge feature has never actually worked on this corpus** — there is no working behaviour to preserve, only the appearance of one.\n\n**HARDEN — `jsonl-loaders.ts` (310 lines), `loadManifestCanonicals` (`cross-author-utils.ts:77-173`), `god_learn.py`'s orchestration, `reason_over_knowledge.py`'s pair machinery, and `compile-corpus-index.py:195-1025` as adapters.**\n\nThis code is genuinely good and rewriting it would be pure risk. The mtime-cache pattern is right; the Zod boundary for KUs and edges is right (`types.ts:93-134` even reports per-record failures with offending field paths); the dropped-line counters at `jsonl-loaders.ts:66-68` and `:103-105` are exactly the observability the rest of the system lacks. The HTTP wiring to the embedding API and Chroma (`smart-retrieval-layer.ts:898-945`) is correct, the `kind: 'query'` asymmetry fix at `:901` was hard-won, and the rerank integration (`:1220-1286`) is well-structured with an AbortController timeout, index validation, and preserved `retrievalScore`. The five parsers at `:195-1025` handle four genuinely different markdown dialects that real analysts produced over a year and they *work* (771 nodes, zero exceptions) — even the one that fails (RDR2 Secondary's `- **Name** — gloss — units · Tier` bullets → 0 nodes) fails by omission, not corruption. **Lift them out as per-format adapters; do not rewrite them.**\n\n**The smallest replacement that preserves the authored content.** The corpus under `corpus/index` — 30.9 MB, 1,848 files, 240 CSVs, 22 manifests, 12 structured ontology JSONs — is the real asset and must not be touched. Concretely:\n\n1. **Invert the source of truth.** Read `*-ontology.json` where present; treat markdown as rendering. Make a missing JSON an *error*, not a silent fallback. This immediately recovers `contributors`, `cross_pipeline_links`, `contested_concepts` and `tension_summary` that the scrape currently loses.\n2. **Lift `:195-1025` out as adapters** (they are already nearly pure functions of `(text, label)`), giving each an offset cursor and an `extra` passthrough for unrecognised keys.\n3. **Rewrite `:1181-1412`** (~250 lines) as a schema-first loader: discover entries from `_synthesis/manifest.json` (22 exist), validate every record, assign stable ids with `(source_path, heading_path, line span, char span)`, refuse to publish on zero-node parses or unexplained count drops, and exit non-zero.\n4. **Shard the artifact per entry** with a manifest; move to SQLite/FTS5 (the repo's existing idiom) for anything claim-level, with an inverted term→claim index and a concept→edge adjacency map so boosting becomes O(terms in chunk) rather than O(total claims).\n5. **Add a CSV adapter** so the 240 files / 20,610 curated edge rows — the densest, most locus-bearing content in the index, currently at 0% runtime reachability — become first-class records.\n\nEstimate: **2–4 weeks**, and it *deletes* more of `compile-corpus-index.py` than it ports. Against that, hardening the CRITICAL/HIGH list alone is ~15 structural items requiring provenance threading through five parsers, a markdown AST to replace `:244-289`/`:335-344`/`:701-724`, a claim/clause record model, and a validation harness — a **larger** diff that arrives without the provenance the current design has no slot for.\n\n**One decisive piece of context.** The docstring at `:14-15` has promised stderr warnings since the file was written, and the mechanism emits **nothing at all** on the live corpus. The design has been failing silently for its entire history with zero observability, and every number in this report had to be recovered by re-running the parsers by hand. That is not a system to tune. **Verdict: the markdown/JSON corpus under `corpus/index` is an excellent foundation. `scripts/compile-corpus-index.py`'s parse-and-emit layer and the TS matching layer are obstacles and should be replaced.**\n\n---\n\n## 8. The dependency-ordered fix list\n\nLegend — **[P]** = prerequisite for claim-level indexing · **[T]** = fixes the system as it stands today.\nNo item depends on a later one.\n\n### Tier 0 — Observability and reproducibility. Nothing else is reviewable until these land.\n\n| # | Fix | path:line | Size | Unblocks | If skipped |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0.1 | **[P][T]** Golden-file test: compile a 5-file fixture corpus into a temp dir, assert exact JSON; plus a schema assertion on the real artifact | new `tests/` (~120 lines) — needs 0.2 first | Every subsequent change becomes reviewable | Every fix below is unverifiable except by manual diff of a 664 KB nondeterministic file. This is why the 10,009-char `centralityTier` survived three feature commits. |\n| 0.2 | **[T]** `argparse` with `--root`/`--out`/`--strict`/`--dry-run`; module `ERRORS` counter incremented inside `warn()`; call `warn()` at all 23 discard sites with path+line; `sys.exit(1)` under `--strict` | `compile-corpus-index.py:30-32`, `:153-154`, `:1361-1412` | 0.1, CI wiring, every diagnosis | The compiler cannot fail. A partial checkout produces a 130-byte skeleton and exit 0. |\n| 0.3 | **[T]** Total sort key `(-len(t), t.lower(), t)`; drop or content-hash `builtAt` | `:1304`, `:1375` | `git diff` becomes a real review surface | 106 of 1,722 positions churn per run; no reviewer can separate content change from seed noise. |\n| 0.4 | **[T]** Atomic write (`.tmp` + `os.replace`) + refuse to publish on 0 nodes or >20% count drop without `--allow-shrink` | `:1383-1387` | safe re-runs | An interrupted write truncates the JSON, which `jsonl-loaders.ts:215` converts to `null` — silent total blackout. |\n| 0.5 | **[T]** Log the `catch` in the index loader with the error and path; distinguish absent/denied/corrupt; log the empty-context case at both `corpus-index-provider.ts:109` and `retrieval-stage.ts:477` | `jsonl-loaders.ts:215-217`; `corpus-index-provider.ts:108-109`; `retrieval-stage.ts:477` | all TS diagnosis | Index missing, index corrupt, and topic-too-short collapse into the same observable: no log line. |\n| 0.6 | **[T]** Wire `npm run typecheck` (`package.json:23`) as a pre-commit/CI gate; fix the 2 arity errors it already reports | `faceted-retrieval.ts:154-164`, `:186-195` | prevents recurrence of the whole 4-arg class | 157 errors accumulate unseen; the entire ICP per-facet retrieval config stays inert. |\n| 0.7 | **[T]** Add `compiled-index.json` count/schema gate to `god-audit.yml` (which already fires on `corpus/**`) | `.github/workflows/god-audit.yml` | CI can see the index at all | **No CI job currently references the compiler or the artifact.** |\n\n### Tier 1 — Stop active corruption. Each is small, each changes shipped output.\n\n| # | Fix | path:line | Size | Unblocks | If skipped |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1.1 | **[T]** Guard both sides of the bridge match: `targetLower.length > 0 && …` | `cross-author-utils.ts:473-474` | bridge feature becomes real | 31 of 72 hooks fire for **every** facet; bridging is noise injection. |\n| 1.2 | **[T]** Refuse to emit a bridge section when either author is `Unknown`/undefined; add explicit fallbacks | `gold-standard-prompt-builder.ts:712-716`, `:1077-1080` | removes the fabrication vector | The prompt orders the model to cite an author named \"Unknown.\" |\n| 1.3 | **[P][T]** Delete `_hooksDerivationDone`; derive lazily per hook (`hook.sourceAuthor ??= …`) | `cross-author-utils.ts:56`, `:342`, `:351` | safe recompiles, safe `projectRoot` | Any recompile renders `(undefined)` in the prompt and kills ICP cross-author backfill after logging success. |\n| 1.4 | **[T]** Make `sourceAuthor`/`targetAuthor` optional in the interface | `cross-author-utils.ts:31-33` | surfaces every unguarded interpolation as a tsc error (needs 0.6) | The type system certifies the bug cannot happen — which is why it survived multiple audits. |\n| 1.5 | **[T]** Use `chunkId` for de-duplication at all 20 sites; add a shared helper | `retrieval-stage.ts:226`, `:303`, `:343`; `pipeline-utils.ts:18`; 16 sites in `write-pipeline-orchestrator.ts` | real multi-query retrieval | The corpus is deduplicated **by page number across every author**, and it worsens with volume. |\n| 1.6 | **[T]** Elision marker in `trimChunkContent` + a fidelity rule rejecting quotes containing it (or make trimming contiguous) | `retrieval-utils.ts:352-370` | citation integrity | Fabricated verbatim quotes that validate at 100%. |\n| 1.7 | **[P][T]** Stop mutating retrieval output: clone on cache set/get; carry `trimmedContent` as a separate field from an immutable `sourceText` | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:303`, `:1430`; `retrieval-stage.ts:305`, `:319`, `:346` | **prerequisite for any offset-based record** | The cache holds lossy derivatives; a daemon drifts from the source each run. Claim offsets into mutable text are meaningless. |\n| 1.8 | **[T]** Reorder `:718-721` so the terminator precedes the continuation arm | `compile-corpus-index.py:718-721` | removes 2 corrupt shipped nodes | 10,009-char `centralityTier`, 973-token units, and `Temporalität` shipping T8's units as its own. |\n| 1.9 | **[T]** Bound the field/value split to its enclosing `## ` section | `compile-corpus-index.py:308-321` | stops 9,867-char absorption | (Note: recovers **zero claims** on its own — see 3.1.) |\n| 1.10 | **[T]** Split node titles on `[—–]` or ` - ` only, never a bare hyphen | `compile-corpus-index.py:350` | correct node names | `Contradiction (PNC)` ships as a primary key; `Being-in-the-world` survives only by file-format accident. |\n| 1.11 | **[T]** `parse_units` splits on `[,;]` only | `compile-corpus-index.py:184-188` | units usable as a join key | 968 tokens are bare English words; `'\\|'` appears 35 times. |\n| 1.12 | **[T]** Merge key `(name.lower(), text)` or per-field provenance; rank tiers and keep max | `compile-corpus-index.py:1319-1348` | honest provenance | 51 cross-book composites attributable to nothing; Part III clusters demote primary sources. |\n| 1.13 | **[T]** `authority_tier` → emit `UNCLASSIFIED`, never default to `secondary`; log the count | `cross-author-utils.ts:317` | primary/secondary integrity | 71 of 117 primary texts labelled secondary scholarship to the model. |\n| 1.14 | **[T]** Add the `u` flag + `\\p{L}` lookarounds to query expansion; word-boundary the canonical-term matcher | `corpus-index-provider.ts:179`; `cross-author-utils.ts:577-578` | Greek reachable; stops εἶδος injection | 16% of the ontology unreachable by script; `information` injects Greek into every embedding. |\n| 1.15 | **[T]** Phase 7 writes `god-reason/phase7-derived-edges.jsonl`; merge becomes the sole writer of `reasoning.jsonl`; merge writes via tmp+rename with a timestamped backup | `reason_over_knowledge.py:449-457`; `god_learn.py:637-645`; `merge-reasoning-edges.py:19`, `:22`, `:206`, `:211-213` | breaks the destructive cycle | `god-learn update` overwrites anchored edges; a second merge run truncates `unanchored-edges.jsonl` from **1,141 → 0**, unrecoverably. |\n| 1.16 | **[T]** Move `deduplicate_manifest` out of `cmd_verify` into an explicit subcommand; tmp+rename; never drop `status='failed'` | `god_learn.py:680-708`, `:711-718` | verify stops mutating its input | (Downgraded from CRITICAL — all 248 removed rows are stale — but a non-atomic in-place rewrite of the ingest ledger by a command named `verify` is still wrong.) |\n| 1.17 | **[T]** Fix the ESM `require` at `quality-integration.ts:749` (static import) | `quality-integration.ts:749-764` | ontology expansion in `detectUnanchoredEdges` | Throws on **every** call, swallowed, so expansion is permanently empty with zero output. |\n\n### Tier 2 — Restore reachability. Content that exists and never arrives.\n\n| # | Fix | path:line | Size | Unblocks | If skipped |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2.1 | **[P][T]** Emit `source`/`target` from Phase 7 (both KU claims are in hand at `:332-335`), or make them optional in the zod schema with `knowledge_ids` as fallback identity — emission-side is correct | `reason_over_knowledge.py:325-338`, `:396-409`; `types.ts:58-62` | **the entire reasoning layer** | `PASS: 0 DROPPED: 5437`. Every edge consumer sees `[]`. |\n| 2.2 | **[T]** Make the contradiction gate report eligibility count; fail if 0 of N were checkable; key on ordered `(source,target)` and print directions | `god_learn.py:70-109`, `:648-661` | a gate that can fire (needs 2.1) | Reports \"no contradictions\" over 5,437 edges it cannot check — reads as a pass. |\n| 2.3 | **[T]** Filesystem discovery of entry directories + per-entry manifest (22 already exist); error on a directory with no manifest; warn on any file yielding 0 nodes | `compile-corpus-index.py:35-133`, `:1185`, `:1200-1227` | 8 uncompiled directories, incl. 3 complete clusters | RDR2 Secondary (12 articles / 506 edges / 65 lemmas) and Phantasia Secondary reach runtime as zero. Adding an entry requires a code edit. |\n| 2.4 | **[T]** Glob hooks corpus-wide, resolve `sourceText` from the owning directory | `compile-corpus-index.py:1238-1244` | non-Aristotle bridges | The \"points of connection\" half of the goal is structurally single-author. |\n| 2.5 | **[T]** Field-alias table for tension normalization (`{node_a,nodeA,pole_A,wendt_position}` / `{node_b,nodeB,pole_B,against}`); warn + counter on no match; `else`/warn at `:1268` | `compile-corpus-index.py:1120-1129`, `:1258-1268` | 55 lost records + 12 silent absences | Four books' entire tension layers — incl. Gross's page-anchored poles and Calleja's `page_anchors` — absent from every prompt. |\n| 2.6 | **[T]** Add `dependencyRelation`/`conflictRelation` to `searchText` **and** to the rendered line | `cross-author-utils.ts:525`; `corpus-index-provider.ts:148`, `:156` | tension layer carries the disagreement | Cheapest high-value fix in the read path. `quality-integration.ts:855` gates on \"tension awareness\" using records the model never saw. |\n| 2.7 | **[T]** Implement `collections` as a metadata `$in` filter (ingest already stamps `collection` at `run_ingest_phase2.py:1742`) | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:194`, `:929-939`; `faceted-retrieval.ts:154-195` | scoped retrieval; fixes `findCrossReferences` and `section-orchestrator` | Reports cross-author agreement using a third author's chunk; \"multi-source\" is one source counted three times. |\n| 2.8 | **[T]** Add a 4th `options` param to `hybridSearch`, thread into both internal searches and `buildCacheKey`, honour `maxChunks`; apply `minRelevance` in `semanticSearch`; normalise merged scores to [0,1] | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:324-377`, `:873-877`; `faceted-retrieval.ts:197` | ICP facet config; stops the 0.857 cliff | Facets starve and `checkScarcity` blames the corpus. |\n| 2.9 | **[T]** Move canonical + KG boosts **before** rerank, or fuse as weighted priors on `retrievalScore`; require word boundaries; log score deltas | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:252-291`, `:583-605`, `:641-642`, `:701` | the reranker's measured win | Two clamped heuristics flatten the cross-encoder to a plateau at 1.0. `\"rede\"` matches inside *Redemption*. |\n| 2.10 | **[T]** Send `top_n: chunks.length`; assert echoed length; gate `rerankActive` on a health probe not the config flag; record rerank status in `pipelineHealth` | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:924-928`, `:1186-1199`, `:1255-1268` | honest retrieval on all 3 dev boxes | Silently unreranked on two of three machines while logs report success; a server `top_n` silently drops 20 of 30 candidates. |\n| 2.11 | **[T]** Throw on non-ok Chroma HTTP; don't cache empty arrays; only latch `collectionResolved` on success; validate `distances` length | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:131-176`, `:210`, `:303`, `:958-970` | the documented F-13 breaker | A briefly-unavailable Chroma yields a fully ungrounded draft reported as successful, with 30 minutes of cached empties. |\n| 2.12 | **[T]** Fold `recordWarning` into `computePipelineHealth`; log the two swallowed paths | `retrieval-stage.ts:241-465`; `stage-types.ts:63-66` | a health signal that means something | A run where every sub-query failed reports `clean`. |\n| 2.13 | **[T]** Add `\"index\"` to `SKIP_DIRS` at all three sites (or point `--root` at a sources subtree) | `run_ingest_phase2.py:978`; `run_ingest.py:365`; `parallel_ingest.py:69` | compile cost stops growing with index size | 516 index markdown files re-chunked and re-embedded on every compile. |\n| 2.14 | **[T]** Precompute `char_ngrams` per KU; give the cross-author pass its own budget; warn loudly on cap | `reason_over_knowledge.py:286-302`, `:349-370` | cross-author reasoning survives the next entry | Already at 86% of budget; one more entry and the cross-author pass silently stops. |\n| 2.15 | **[T]** Return direction from `infer_relation`; score marker families instead of first-match; word-boundary the markers | `reason_over_knowledge.py:121-156`, `:319` | correct graph traversal | ~half of asymmetric edges point backwards; `\"by means of\"` creates `defined_as`. |\n| 2.16 | **[T]** Resolve `_hook_licensed_pairs` path from `__file__` or `--index`; log resolved path + pair count; catch specific exceptions; count dropped hooks | `reason_over_knowledge.py:190-214` | CWD-independent runs | Hook-licensed edges silently disabled by the caller's CWD; 31 of 72 hooks dropped uncounted. |\n| 2.17 | **[T]** Fix `deriveAuthor`: resolve the dash branch through the manifest; require word-boundary matches; reject ambiguous hits | `cross-author-utils.ts:395-403` | cross-author ChromaDB backfill for non-Aristotle | `'Heidegger'` ≠ manifest `'Heidegger, Martin'` → zero rows, no flag. Works today only because every hook is Aristotle. |\n| 2.18 | **[T]** Single shared min-word-length constant between producer and consumers; exempt canonical terms regardless of length | `cross-author-utils.ts:613` vs `:461`, `:517` | `soul`, `body`, `nous`, `time`, `form` | The four-letter core vocabulary is structurally excluded, and it looks like \"no bridge is relevant.\" |\n| 2.19 | **[T]** Delete the private `protectedTerms` cache; delegate to `loadCompiledIndex()`; add `path` to `_authorKUIndexCache`; add `size` to all cache keys | `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:794-800`; `jsonl-loaders.ts:205-206`, `:224` | one consistent view of one file | Terms frozen for the process lifetime; cross-project contamination. |\n| 2.20 | **[T]** Fix MLA citation validation: explicit `(Surname NN)` parse, ≥3-char prefix match, validate the page against `source.pages`, `\\p{L}` for non-ASCII; include title in the manifest dedup predicate | `corpus-constraint-builder.ts:110-121`, `:295-324` | citation rigor | `(Barrett 471)` passes on a 300-page book; a real corpus work is flagged as a hallucination. |\n\n### Tier 3 — Claim-level indexing. Everything here needs Tier 0–2.\n\n| # | Fix | path:line | Size | Unblocks | If skipped |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 3.1 | **[P]** Thread an offset cursor `(path, line, char)` through all five parsers and every call site; emit `{id, source_path, heading_path, line_start, line_end, char_start, char_end}` on every record | `compile-corpus-index.py:195-1025`, `:379-390`, `:495-506`, `:663-674`, `:756-767` | **everything below** | **The single largest obstacle to the goal.** Claim records are span-anchored by definition; a schema with no span cannot hold them. Note: fixing 1.9 alone recovers *zero* claims without this. |\n| 3.2 | **[P]** `extra` passthrough for unrecognised keys at every emit site | `:344`, `:756-767`, `:1165-1174` | unanticipated claim fields; 13 tension keys; `global_candidate` | The compiler demonstrably parses tension structure and Key Positions and throws them away for lack of a slot. **This alone would have made the whole bug class visible on day one.** |\n| 3.3 | **[P]** Invert the source of truth: read the **12 `*-ontology.json`** files; markdown becomes rendering; missing JSON is an error | `compile-corpus-index.py:1196-1227` | `contributors`, `cross_pipeline_links`, `contested_concepts`, `tension_summary` | The pipeline keeps recovering structure from prose while the structure sits in the same directory. |\n| 3.4 | **[P]** Heading-tree/block parser replacing the line-scanners; tables as typed rows routed by column signature, not heading spelling | `:244-289`, `:335-344`, `:533-620`, `:701-724` | 37.6% discarded preamble; 7 `### N.` contested-node sections; 153 out-of-window rows | Column identity remains a substring guess; one blank line still deletes a row. |\n| 3.5 | **[P]** Promote Key Positions / Tensions / contested nodes to first-class record types with their own schemas | new (~150-250 lines) | **claim-level records** | The 14 numbered Key Positions with Bekker loci stay absorbed and dropped. |\n| 3.6 | **[P]** CSV adapter covering all ~70 header shapes; promote `locus`, `book_page`, `page_anchor` to first-class fields | new; replaces `normalize-edges.py` entirely | **240 files / 20,610 curated edge rows, currently 0% reachable** | The densest, most locus-bearing content in the index stays invisible to every runtime system. |\n| 3.7 | **[P]** Resolve edge endpoints to node ids at build time (exact → alias → transliteration); warn on unresolved; `nodes: [...]` list instead of `nodeA`/`nodeB` | `:1165-1174` | a traversable graph; triadic tensions | 52 of 64 edges reference nothing; \"every point of connection\" cannot be counted or contradiction-checked. |\n| 3.8 | **[P]** Multi-match, boundary-correct concept resolver: one compiled alternation (or Aho-Corasick); return **all** matched concepts with spans; key lookup on `.lower()` with a total sort | replaces `merge-reasoning-edges.py:52-76` | claims linked to every concept they invoke | One concept per claim (26 claims → `Perception`); 218 of 1,463 terms unmatchable; ~289 s → ~80 h at 100x. |\n| 3.9 | **[P]** Shard the artifact per entry with a manifest; SQLite/FTS5 + vector sidecar for claim/clause records; inverted term→claim index and concept→edge adjacency | `:1384-1387`; `jsonl-loaders.ts:89`, `:210`; `smart-retrieval-layer.ts:586-596`, `:618-638` | 100x volume | Hard walls: `MAX_STRING_LENGTH` at 24.97x; ~2.8 GB heap per parse at clause level; ~120M KG-boost iterations per sub-query. |\n| 3.10 | **[P]** Streaming NDJSON readers (`readline`) with explicit parsed/dropped counters | `jsonl-loaders.ts:89`, `:210` | removes the 24.97x wall and the 150 ms → 3.75 s main-thread block | Two different undiagnosable failures — uncaught `RangeError` vs silent `null`. |\n| 3.11 | **[P]** Token-budgeted selection replacing absolute caps; log `emitted/scored`; sentence-boundary truncation with an ellipsis; `[a, b, c, +N more]` for units | `corpus-index-provider.ts:101-127` | context scales with the corpus | Caps are absolute: at 100x the emitted context is byte-identical while discard goes 82% → 99.8%. |\n| 3.12 | **[P]** Replace substring scoring with embedding similarity against the existing vector store; field-weighted fallback (name > transliteration > aliases > definition) with `u`-flag boundaries and length normalisation | `corpus-index-provider.ts:81-91`; `cross-author-utils.ts:469-530` | ranking worth capping | Ranking is dominated by definition length; at 100x, incidental-substring records squeeze out the canonical ones entirely. |\n| 3.13 | **[P]** Single shared `types/compiled-index.ts`, Zod-derived so schema and type cannot drift; `.safeParse` at `jsonl-loaders.ts:211` with per-record drop counts | `corpus-index-provider.ts:29-50`; `cross-author-utils.ts:20-45`; `jsonl-loaders.ts:198`, `:211` | schema enforcement across all consumers | Three duplicate declarations with divergent shapes mean tsc cannot check any consumer against the real schema — the structural precondition for the `sourceAuthor: string` unsoundness. **A 10-line schema here converts six CRITICALs into startup warnings.** |\n| 3.14 | **[P]** Scope `buildCorpusCatalog` to section-relevant authors, or emit author-level counts with drill-down; backfill `author_raw`/`title_raw` in the manifest | `cross-author-utils.ts:159-167`, `:307-331` | 461 of 578 unreachable titles; the ~90x prompt wall | The catalog declares 80% of the corpus non-existent **and** blows the context window at ~90x. |\n| 3.15 | **[P]** Compute `QuoteSpan` offsets and hashes against immutable `sourceText` (needs 1.7); hash exactly `sentence.text`; add `clean_text`/`source_kind` to `ContextChunk` for real | `faceted-retrieval.ts:289-290`, `:318-330` | clause-level provenance | Offsets point into a collage; every span reports as stale. |\n\n**Critical-path summary.** 0.2 → 0.1 → 0.3 gate everything. 1.3, 1.5, 1.7 are the three cheap TS fixes with the widest blast radius. 2.1 is the highest value-per-line item in the entire report — one schema alignment resurrects a 5,437-edge graph that is currently 100% dead. And **3.1 is the gate for the entire programme**: without a provenance triple on every record, nothing above claim-level is achievable, and no amount of work in Tiers 1–2 moves toward it."
  },
